_time_value_ranking.md:243:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n./analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md:250:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n./analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md:257:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:24:### A1. PurpleRiver Mini 640 — BEST OVERALL PICK\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:79:- Thinner module (17.3mm) than PurpleRiver (21mm)\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:82:- Price not listed — requires inquiry, expected competitive with PurpleRiver\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:109:- Self-developed 12µm core (likely from the same Chinese foundries as PurpleRiver/VCAN)\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:145:- Higher power (0.9W) than PurpleRiver (0.5W) but still well under 4.5W\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:151:**Verdict: ✅ Viable option if ~$400–$550. Higher weight and power than PurpleRiver but still within limits.**\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:172:- Often identical specifications to PurpleRiver/VCAN modules\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:358:| **PurpleRiver Mini 640** | $399 | ~$60 | ~$20 | **~$479** | ✅ (21% margin) |\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:372:| PurpleRiver Mini 640 | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ (13mm) | ✅ | CVBS+USB | Medium (Alibaba) |\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:388:**1. PurpleRiver Mini 640 with 13mm lens** (~$479 total)\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_market_analysis.md:426:1. **Contact PurpleRiver** for live single-unit pricing with 13mm lens + CVBS adapter + shipping\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_trade_study.md:33:| **PurpleRiver Mini 640** | **$399 – $1,620** | **< 20 g** | **≤ 50 mK** | **CVBS, USB, MIPI** | **31.9°×25.7°** | **✅ Base config at $399** |\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_trade_study.md:38:### PurpleRiver Mini 640 — Most Promising Candidate\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_trade_study.md:86:If the PurpleRiver Mini 640 base module costs ~$450 with a 13mm lens:\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_trade_study.md:113:1. **Verify PurpleRiver module specs** — confirm NETD ≤ 50 mK, actual available lens options (13mm = ~32° HFOV is ideal), and ability to order single units at the ~$399 base price\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/camera_trade_study.md:114:2. **If PurpleRiver doesn't pan out:** The Axisflying GE-3F at $680 may be negotiable for single-unit purchase, or we could consider a 384×288 sensor as a cost-down option\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/thermal_camera_market_analysis.md:108:All **CVBS-output modules** (T8-T13) can connect to any analog VTX in the VTX CSV (V1-V11) for live FPV downlink. The same modules also have **USB output** for connecting to the SBC for onboard recording and analysis — which is the Phase 3 architecture we already decided on.\n./analysis/market_analyses_and_research/thermal_camera_market_analysis.md:112:Thermal Camera (T8-T13)\n./analysis/openhd-air-wifi-adapter-trade-study.md:22:| Cost | Minimize — already using budget on T13 ($590) and SBC3 ($126) |\n./README.md:27:- ✅ **Airframe — iFlight Chimera9 ECO (9\")** · ✅ **Thermal — PurpleRiver Mini 640 (640×512, USB)** · ✅ **SBC — NanoPi M5 (RK3576)**\n./README.md:97:- **Design locks:** the sweep fixes the thermal (`T13`), SBC (`SBC3`), and airframe (`AF3a`/`AF3b`, Chimera9 ECO) to the locked selections via `FIXED_*` constants (set to `None` to re-open a dimension).\n./candidates.sysml:1132:  part T13 : CameraSubsystem {\n./candidates.sysml:1133:   :>> name = \"PurpleRiver Mini 640\";\n./candidates.sysml:1135:   :>> brand = \"PurpleRiver\";\n./candidates.sysml:1136:   :>> cost_USD = 590.00;            // 350-550\n./candidates.sysml:1713:  // (need >= ~25 fps for the T13 25 Hz feed). R4_SBC_VIDEO_PROC has no executable check.\n./candidates.sysml:1809:   :>> videoProtocolIn = \"USB UVC 1.1 (← T13 thermal cam)\";\n./candidates.sysml:3457:   :>> energy = 959040.0 [J];    // 22.2 V × 12 Ah × 3600\n./candidates.sysml:3477:   :>> energy = 959040.0 [J];    // 22.2 V × 12 Ah × 3600\n./candidates.sysml:3556:  part BAT13 : Battery {\n./candidates.sysml:3560:   :>> mass = 590.0 [g];\n./candidates.sysml:3750:   :>> energy = 959040.0 [J];     // 22.2 V × 12 Ah × 3600\n./candidates.sysml:3770:   :>> energy = 959040.0 [J];     // 22.2 V × 12 Ah × 3600\n./BOM.md:40:| PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm) | `T13` | [thermal-image.com](https://www.thermal-image.com/product/mini-640-uncooled-lwir-thermal-camera-module/) | $590.00 |\n./BOM.md:72:- **Refine Phase 2 pricing** — confirm actual purchase prices for T13 thermal camera, DVR9, WLAN_AIR1, WLAN_GND1, and Foxeer Echo 2 Max antennas; update candidates.sysml cost_USD and BOM subtotal accordingly.\n./reference/cad-resources.md:48:### C. PurpleRiver Mini 640 — thermal camera (`T13`)\n./reference/cad-resources.md:50:- **Official doc:** [Mini 640 specifications PDF](https://www.thermal-image.com/download/purpleriver-mini640-thermal-camera-specifications/) (≈140 KB).\n./reference/cad-resources.md:51:- **Verified dimensions:** body **21 × 21 mm** (without lens), **< 20 g**; lens options 4–75 mm — **T13 uses the 13 mm lens**. Trivial to model: a 21 × 21 × ~21 mm body box + a ~Ø13–16 mm lens barrel. (NB: `candidates.sysml` currently lists T13 as `~17x17x35` — reconcile to the vendor's 21 × 21 mm body.)\n./reference/cad-resources.md:121