{"type":"message","id":"b3101df5","parentId":"14fe5c90","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:15:43.493Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to move the SBC procurement from Phase 3 into Phase 2 (replacing the DVR's slot), and drop the DVR entirely. Let me understand the current phases:\n\n**Current phase structure:**\n- Phase 1 — Basic flight + FPV downlink + waypoints\n- Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink (includes DVR9)\n- Phase 3 — On-board SBC detection + autonomous route modification (includes SBC3)\n\nThe SBC (NanoPi M5, `SBC3`, $126) and its mount/cooling (~$15) are currently in Phase 3. The DVR (Monster UVC Recorder, `DVR9`, $129) is in Phase 2.\n\nThe user wants to:\n1. Drop the DVR from Phase 2\n2. Move the SBC + mount/cooling from Phase 3 into Phase 2\n3. Phase 3 becomes empty or gets redefined\n\nThis makes a lot of sense architecturally — the SBC can do onboard recording via USB from the T13 thermal camera, making a separate DVR redundant.\n\nLet me think about what documents need updating:\n\n1. **BOM.md** — Move SBC3 + mount from Phase 3 to Phase 2, remove DVR9 from Phase 2, update subtotals and totals\n2. **candidates.sysml** — May need to update compatibility or notes\n3. **SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md** — Phase assignment changes\n4. **README.md** — Phase descriptions\n5. **systems_engineering_plan.md** — Phase plan\n6. Any other documents that reference phase assignments\n\nLet me check what the current phase structure looks like in the various docs.\n\nLet me start by reading the relevant files to understand the full scope of changes needed.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Understood. That's a clean architectural move — the SBC handles onboard recording via USB from the T13, making the standalone DVR redundant. Let me scope out what needs updating.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_572a1267ce9c4743af344012","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7bbe63dcb70846a69b9828a0","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rn \"Phase 2\\|Phase 3\\|Phase 1\\|SBC3\\|DVR9\\|procurement phase\" --include=\"*.md\" --include=\"*.sysml\" . | grep -v \"flight_time\\|\\.git\\|node_modules\\|analysis/\" | head -40"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rn \\\"Phase 2\\\\|Phase 3\\\\|Phase 1\\\\|SBC3\\\\|DVR9\\\\|procurement phase\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.sysml\\\" . | grep -v \\\"flight_time\\\\|\\\\.git\\\\|node_modules\\\\|analysis/\\\" | head -40\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":35835,"output":609,"cacheRead":1024,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":394,"totalTokens":37468,"cost":{"input":0.0035835,"output":0.00012179999999999999,"cacheRead":0.00002048,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0037257799999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783264533052,"responseId":"gen-1783264533-u9f212A892CVfUZ36o0I"}}
{"type":"message","id":"d2fe9c3e","parentId":"b3101df5","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:15:43.543Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_572a1267ce9c4743af344012","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Bill of Materials (BOM) — Thermal Surveillance Drone\n\nFull procurement list, **sorted by build phase** with a subtotal per phase. Derived from\n[`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md) (selections) and\n[`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml) (names, IDs, links, costs). **Part #** = the model\ncandidate ID (the project's internal part number). Three phases (the old Phase 1 basic\nflight + Phase 2 FPV/waypoints are now a single Phase 1).\n\n_Generated 2026-07-01. Costs are current best estimates (USD); confirm at purchase._\n\n> **Flight battery = `BAT10`** (Upgrade Energy 6S 12 Ah Amprius) — `BAT09` is out of stock.\n> **2× `BAT22`** (GNB) are procured as development/shakedown packs (spare the Amprius on early flights).\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Basic flight + FPV downlink + waypoints\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|--:|\n| iFlight Chimera9 ECO 6S (9\", PNP) + **GPS pre-installed** | `AF3a` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/Chimera9-ECO-6S-Pro2068) | $457.99 |\n| HQ 9X4X3 props — 4-pack (extra set) | — | shop.iflight.com / HQ | $17.00 |\n| iFlight True Diversity ELRS receiver | `iFlightTD` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/) | $31.99 |\n| RadioMaster TX12 Mark II ELRS radio | `TX5` | [radiomasterrc.com](https://www.radiomasterrc.com/products/tx12) | $117.93 |\n| HGLRC Hermes ELRS SIM USB Dongle — primary laptop control + telemetry | `TLM2` | [amazon.com](https://www.amazon.com/s?k=HGLRC+Hermes+ELRS+USB+dongle) | $16.00 |\n| Battery **(flight)** — Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S3P 12 Ah Amprius | `BAT10` | [upgrade-energy.com](https://www.upgrade-energy.com/) | $275.00 |\n| Battery **(development, ×2)** — GNB 6S3P 12 Ah 21700 Li-ion | `BAT22` | [gaoneng.shop](https://www.gaoneng.shop/products/gaoneng-gnb-6s-22.2v-12000mah-10c-xt60-li-ion-battery-made-with-li-ion-lithium-ion-21700) | $220.00 |\n| Skydroid 5.8 GHz 150CH UVC receiver (**dual antenna**) | `VRX6` | [alibaba.com](https://www.alibaba.com/product-detail/SKYDROID-5-8GHz-FPV-Receiver-UVC_1601393061166.html) *(select dual-antenna variant; confirm price at checkout)* | ~$44.45 |\n| TrueRC X-AIR 5.8 MK II RHCP patch antenna | `PATCH1` | [truerc.com](https://truerc.com/63425-x-air-58-mk-ii-rp-sma) | $36.85 |\n| iFlight Anti Spark Filter (XT60, 150 A) | `ASF1` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/index.php?route=product/product&product_id=3474) | $14.99 |\n| HOTA D6 Pro battery charger | `CHG1` | [hotarc.com](https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0FLXL4SZW/ref=ox_sc_act_image_1?smid=A10OEFIP1P2D8&th=1) | $111.55 |\n| USB-A→USB-C adapter (MacBook Air) | — | generic | $11.00 |\n| FPV camera + 5.8 GHz analog VTX | *(bundled w/ `AF3a`)* | — | $0.00 |\n| GCS laptop (existing MacBook Air) | — | — | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 1 subtotal** | | | **$1,354.75** |\n\n## Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|--:|\n| PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm) | `T13` | [thermal-image.com](https://www.thermal-image.com/product/mini-640-uncooled-lwir-thermal-camera-module/) | $650.00 |\n| Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) | `DVR9` | [amazon.com](https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Monster+UVC+Recorder) | $129.00 |\n| LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 RTL8812EU bare WiFi module (air side) + USB-A stub + 2× u.fl→RP-SMA pigtails | `WLAN_AIR1` | [aliexpress.com](https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005007098141054.html) | ~$20.00 |\n| Alfa AWUS036ACH RTL8812AU USB-C WiFi adapter (ground side) | `WLAN_GND1` | [rokland.com](https://store.rokland.com/products/alfa-awus036ach-usb-c-802-11ac-ac1200-dual-band-high-power-wifi-usb-adapter) | $65.00 |\n| Foxeer Echo 2 Max 5.8 GHz linear patch antenna × 2 (ground diversity, 60° beam, RP-SMA male) | `ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2` | [foxeer.com](https://www.foxeer.com/foxeer-echo-2-max-high-gain-antenna-g-434) | $60.00 |\n| VMware Fusion (ground station VM — free personal use) | — | vmware.com | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$924.00** |\n\n## Phase 3 — On-board SBC detection + autonomous route modification\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|--:|\n| NanoPi M5, 4 GB SBC (Rockchip RK3576) | `SBC3` | [friendlyelec.com](https://www.friendlyelec.com/index.php?route=product/product&path=69&product_id=309) | $126.00 |\n| SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + 30 mm fan + heat-set hardware) | — | fabricated ([reference/cad-resources.md](reference/cad-resources.md)) | ~$15.00 |\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$141.00** |\n\n---\n\n## Totals\n\n| Phase | Subtotal |\n|---|--:|\n| Phase 1 — flight + FPV + waypoints | $1,354.75 |\n| Phase 2 — thermal + recording + OpenHD digital downlink | ~$924.00 |\n| Phase 3 — SBC autonomy | $141.00 |\n| **Grand total (all procurement)** | **~$2,419.75** |\n\n**R4 integrated-system cost ≈ $2,088** (≤ $2,500 ✓) — the grand total minus **reusable/support\nitems not part of the per-drone flight system**: the 2× `BAT22` development packs ($220) and\nthe `CHG1` charger ($100). Both totals are under the $2,500 R4 cap.\n\n## Next steps\n- **Phase 2 pricing** — T13 updated to $650.00 ($590 base + $60 shipping, confirmed 2026-07-05). Remaining items: confirm actual purchase prices for DVR9, WLAN_AIR1, WLAN_GND1, and Foxeer Echo 2 Max antennas; update candidates.sysml cost_USD and BOM subtotal accordingly.\n- **Refine Phase 3 pricing** — confirm NanoPi M5 current price and SBC mount/cooling materials cost; update candidates.sysml and BOM subtotal.\n- Recompute grand total and R4 system cost once Phase 2 + 3 prices are confirmed.\n\n## Notes\n- **Part # = model candidate ID** (the internal part number in [`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml)); \"—\" = no catalog part yet (generic/fabricated/TBD).\n- **Battery:** `BAT10` is the flight default (`BAT09` out of stock); the **2× `BAT22`** are development/shakedown packs (cheap, robust — fly these first, spare the Amprius).\n- **Bundled at $0:** the FPV camera + analog VTX ship with the Chimera9 ECO PNP. **GPS is now pre-installed** (iFlight BLITZ M10 GPS V2 Mini, `G4`; cost folded into the airframe line at $457.99 incl. shipping). **Existing at $0:** the MacBook Air GCS.\n- **TBD lines:** the flight-controller firmware (ArduPilot/PX4 vs Betaflight — a configuration choice, no cost).\n- The flight-time sweep reports ~$1,690 for the drone + GCS using *cost-representative* RX/radio; this BOM uses the **actual selected** parts (iFlight TD RX + TX12 MkII radio) plus GPS, dongle, charger, adapter, dev batteries, and the SBC mount — hence the higher, complete figure.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783264543543}}
{"type":"message","id":"74650f60","parentId":"d2fe9c3e","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:15:43.544Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7bbe63dcb70846a69b9828a0","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"./MODEL_ISSUES.md:139:   (Mission Planner / QGroundControl tuning profiles) and the Phase 3 SBC MAVLink\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:141:   is decided. **Action needed:** pick ArduPilot or PX4 before Phase 1 first flight\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:301:      DVR9, so **14 of 16 thermals are now viable**. Only T7 (raw SPI) and T16 (raw\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:306:      used only in the earlier (Phase 1-3) stages, so it is no longer a flight-time\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:335:      laptop is the ground station. **PRIMARY (Phase 2+):** an ELRS USB dongle\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:337:      laptop. **BACKUP / Phase 1:** a cheap handheld ELRS radio for manual control\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:422:    constraint — the **90×62 mm NanoPi M5 footprint** is. **Result (T13+SBC3,\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:443:    budget.** Pulled the video downlink forward into Phase 1 (the Chimera9 PNP already\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:472:    - **Phase restructure (4 → 3):** merged old Phase 1 (basic flight) + Phase 2\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:473:      (FPV/waypoints) into a single **Phase 1**, and **pulled GPS + the ELRS laptop\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:474:      dongle into Phase 1**. Old Phase 3 (thermal + DVR) → **Phase 2**; old Phase 4\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:475:      (SBC) → **Phase 3**. The DVR is now a Phase 1–2 part; the SBC records at Phase 3.\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:4:the old Phase 1 \"basic flight\" and Phase 2 \"FPV + waypoints\" are now a single Phase 1).\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:8:## Phase 1 — Basic Flight + FPV Downlink + Waypoints\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:45:## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + Onboard Recording\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:48:**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:50:- ThermalVideoRecorder — **Monster UVC Recorder** (`DVR9`, standalone USB-UVC DVR to microSD)\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:52:**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera and DVR.\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:65:## Phase 3 — On-Board Detection + Autonomous Route Modification\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:68:**New Components (vs Phase 2)**\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:69:- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU)\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:72:**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 2, plus the SBC (the SBC records at this stage, so the DVR is no longer required).\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:37:### 6. Onboard Recording Architecture Decision (Phase 3)\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:38:- **Decision:** Phase 3 will store thermal footage onboard via an inline DVR, not rely solely on live downlink\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:41:- This eliminates need for second VTX for thermal in Phase 3\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:42:- **ThermalVideoRecorder** (inline DVR) added to systems_engineering_plan.md Phase 3 components and to model.md as a new `part def`\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:71:| Thermal downlink (Phase 3) | **Onboard recording via inline DVR** | Eliminates second VTX, survives signal loss, ~$20-30 part, negligible weight |\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:75:| GPS priority | **Critical for Phase 2 (waypoints)** | Budget +$25 if airframe doesn't include one |\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:82:2. **Update systems_engineering_plan.md Phase 2 components** — RadioReceiver now handles telemetry; Phase 2 should reflect this (no separate telemetry hardware)\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:87:7. **Phase 3 DVR selection** — Pick a specific inline DVR model for the ThermalVideoRecorder\n./session-handoffs/2026-06-10.md:95:- **systems_engineering_plan.md** — Phase 3/4 updated to include ThermalVideoRecorder\n./session-handoffs/260511_1.md:15:- Maintain $2,500 total cost constraint throughout design Phase 2.\n./session-handoffs/260511_1.md:20:- Proceed with Phase 2 architecture development guided by complete requirements.\n./model.sysml:631: doc /* GPS module providing position, velocity, and time data to the flight controller. Critical for return-to-home and autonomous waypoint navigation (Phase 1+). May be pre-installed with some airframe packages. */\n./model.sysml:760: doc /* Inline DVR that records analog CVBS video to microSD card while passing video through to the VTX. Enables onboard storage of thermal footage without requiring the SBC (Phase 3). Survives RF signal loss — footage is on the card regardless of downlink quality. */\n./model.sysml:823: PRIMARY bidirectional control + telemetry link for Phase 1+ autonomous operation,\n./model.sysml:850: doc /* Air-side WiFi adapter for OpenHD/WFB-ng digital video downlink (Phase 2+).\n./model.sysml:917: // PRIMARY (Phase 1+): ELRS USB dongle to the laptop carries control + telemetry.\n./model.sysml:919: // BACKUP / Phase 1: handheld ELRS radio for manual control if the laptop fails.\n./model.sysml:924: // Phase 2+: OpenHD digital thermal video downlink ground node"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":33,"aggregated":"./MODEL_ISSUES.md:139:   (Mission Planner / QGroundControl tuning profiles) and the Phase 3 SBC MAVLink\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:141:   is decided. **Action needed:** pick ArduPilot or PX4 before Phase 1 first flight\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:301:      DVR9, so **14 of 16 thermals are now viable**. Only T7 (raw SPI) and T16 (raw\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:306:      used only in the earlier (Phase 1-3) stages, so it is no longer a flight-time\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:335:      laptop is the ground station. **PRIMARY (Phase 2+):** an ELRS USB dongle\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:337:      laptop. **BACKUP / Phase 1:** a cheap handheld ELRS radio for manual control\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:422:    constraint — the **90×62 mm NanoPi M5 footprint** is. **Result (T13+SBC3,\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:443:    budget.** Pulled the video downlink forward into Phase 1 (the Chimera9 PNP already\n.