{"type":"message","id":"3e5b9b3e","parentId":"74650f60","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:16:09.314Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_070c10dff264468faa99c688","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/systems_engineering_plan.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"path\":\"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/systems_engineering_plan.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_deee2d498b424907a8024679","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md","limit":60,"offset":52},"partialArgs":"{\"path\":\"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md\",\"limit\":60,\"offset\":52}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":40724,"output":156,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":0,"totalTokens":40880,"cost":{"input":0.0040723999999999995,"output":0.0000312,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0041036}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783264543546,"responseId":"gen-1783264544-YYXCx7vHed9woTuuDqI6"}}
{"type":"message","id":"6bbf601a","parentId":"3e5b9b3e","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:16:09.333Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_070c10dff264468faa99c688","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# System Engineering Plan\n\nThe build proceeds in **three incremental phases** (merged from the original four —\nthe old Phase 1 \"basic flight\" and Phase 2 \"FPV + waypoints\" are now a single Phase 1).\nSelected parts: [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md); full phased bill of\nmaterials: [`BOM.md`](BOM.md).\n\n## Phase 1 — Basic Flight + FPV Downlink + Waypoints\n**Goal** — Stable manual line-of-sight flight, live analog video on the laptop, and\npre-programmed waypoint missions.\n\n**Requirements**\n- R4_AF_PAYLOAD, R4_AF_WT, R4_AF_ASSY, R4_AF_STIFF, R4_AF_LANDING, R4_AF_COST, R4_AF_PROP_CFG, R4_AF_PWR_DIST\n- R4_BAT_VOLT, R4_BAT_WT, R4_BAT_IF\n- R4_GCS_VIDEO_DISP, R4_GCS_RANGE, R4_GCS_IF, R4_GCS_CTRL, R4_GCS_TELEM\n\n**Components Required**\n- Airframe — **iFlight Chimera9 ECO 9\" PNP** (`AF3a`); bundles a 5.8 GHz analog VTX + FPV camera (air-side video, $0)\n- RadioReceiver — **iFlight True Diversity ELRS** (`iFlightTD`); RC control + telemetry on one link\n- Battery — **Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S3P 12 Ah Amprius** (`BAT10`, flight default) + **2× GNB 6S3P 12 Ah** (`BAT22`, development packs)\n- RadioControlTransmitter — **RadioMaster Boxer ELRS** (`TX1`, handheld)\n- ELRS USB dongle — primary laptop control + telemetry link (TBD)\n- GPS — **TBS M10** (`G6`) for waypoint navigation\n- VideoReceiver — **Skydroid 150CH 5.8 GHz UVC** (`VRX6`); laptop-direct video\n- Antenna — **TrueRC X-AIR 5.8 patch** (`PATCH1`); video-link range margin (see `analysis/rf_link_budget.md`)\n- Anti-spark filter — **iFlight Anti Spark** (`ASF1`, XT60 inline)\n- Battery charger — **HOTA D6 Pro** (`CHG1`, 6S Li-ion/LiPo, bench/reusable)\n- GCS laptop (MacBook — existing equipment, $0)\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Power-on and bind the ELRS receiver to the handheld + the laptop ELRS dongle.\n2. Flash ArduPilot/PX4 onto the flight controller; configure the GPS.\n3. Calibrate sensors (compass, accelerometer, gyro).\n4. Configure arming, failsafe, and return-to-launch (RTL) behavior.\n5. Basic flight-envelope tests (hover, pitch, roll, yaw) in LOS.\n6. Connect the Skydroid VRX (USB/UVC) + patch antenna to the laptop; view & record live video in QuickTime/OBS.\n7. Confirm live analog FPV feed + telemetry to the laptop (QGroundControl).\n8. Define a waypoint mission in QGroundControl; upload and execute with FPV monitoring and manual ELRS override.\n9. Validate position-hold and RTL.\n\n**Result** — Ready-to-fly airframe under manual LOS control with live laptop video and autonomous waypoint routes.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + Onboard Recording\n**Goal** — Mount the thermal camera, record onboard to microSD, and downlink live thermal video.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\n- Thermal Camera Subsystem — **PurpleRiver Mini 640** (`T13`, 640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm lens, USB)\n- ThermalVideoRecorder — **Monster UVC Recorder** (`DVR9`, standalone USB-UVC DVR to microSD)\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera and DVR.\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Mount the thermal camera on the airframe (clear FOV, nose/chin) and power from the airframe rail.\n2. Route the thermal video → DVR (records to microSD) and to the laptop (live view).\n3. Configure the DVR to auto-start recording on power-up (per-flight files).\n4. Fly and recover thermal footage from microSD post-flight (footage survives RF loss).\n5. Confirm live thermal downlink on the laptop and Johnson detect/recognize performance at 90–120 m.\n\n**Result** — Thermal video recorded onboard (survives signal loss) with live downlink; meets the R3 detection/recognition requirements.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — On-Board Detection + Autonomous Route Modification\n**Goal** — Add on-board AI thermal detection/classification and dynamic mission adaptation.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 2)**\n- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU)\n- SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + fan — see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md))\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 2, plus the SBC (the SBC records at this stage, so the DVR is no longer required).\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Mount the SBC on a 3D-printed deck; connect to the airframe rail and the flight controller (UART/MAVLink).\n2. Route the thermal camera video → SBC (USB-UVC).\n3. Deploy the INT8-quantized detection/classification model via the RKNN toolchain (RKNPU2); verify ≥ ~25 fps.\n4. Map detections to MAVLink commands (loiter/adjust on a target); modify the mission in-flight.\n5. Validate fallback: if the SBC fails, the drone completes the current waypoint and RTLs.\n\n**Result** — Autonomous drone that detects and reacts to thermal targets, meeting all SBC and camera requirements.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783264569333}}
{"type":"message","id":"2862b47c","parentId":"6bbf601a","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:16:09.333Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_deee2d498b424907a8024679","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n### Airframe variant — RESOLVED: PNP (`AF3a`) + GPS pre-installed\nChose the **PNP** variant + **GPS pre-install option** (+$39). All-up airframe mass = 729 g (~$386; no bundled receiver). External ELRS RX added separately. The airframe **bundles a BLITZ Whoop 5.8 GHz analog VTX + analog CMOS FPV camera + iFlight BLITZ M10 GPS V2 Mini** (so VTX, FPV-cam, and GPS selections are all decided by the airframe). Shared drivetrain: XING-E 2809 800KV · BLITZ F7 FC · BLITZ E55 55 A 4-in-1 ESC · HQ 9×4×3 props.\n\n### Battery power interface — standardized on **XT60** (refined 2026-06-30)\nThe battery↔drone power interface is now modeled: `model.sysml` `BatteryPowerInterface` gained a **`ConnectorCompatible`** constraint, the power ports (`PowerSourcePort`/`PowerSinkPort`) carry a `connector` attribute, and `Airframe` gained `batteryConnector`. **The whole power chain is XT60:** battery → iFlight anti-spark (XT60) → Chimera9 ECO XT60 lead. Verified against the candidates — **BAT09 / BAT10 / BAT22 (the three contenders) are all XT60** ✓; only non-contenders differ (**BAT08 = XT90**, **BAT23 Tattu LiPo = EC5** → would need an adapter). Chargers (below) output XT60 or use an XT60 charge lead.\n\n---\n\n## 🔶 OPEN / in-progress\n\n| Role | Status | ID(s) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **On-board DVR** | open (**Phase 2**) | `DVR9` (rep.) | **Phase 1–2 only** — at the SBC stage (**Phase 3**) the SBC records; the DVR is costed/compatibility-checked but not in the SBC-stage flight-time. |\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 build (selected) — flight + FPV downlink + waypoints\n| Item | Part | ~Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| Airframe + GPS (bundled) | Chimera9 ECO PNP + BLITZ M10 GPS V2 Mini (`AF3a` + `G4`) | $386 |\n| Extra props | HQ 9X4X3 — 4-pack | $17 |\n| Receiver | iFlight True Diversity ELRS (`iFlightTD`) | $30 |\n| Handheld radio | RadioMaster TX12 Mark II ELRS (`TX5`) | $118 |\n| ELRS USB dongle (primary laptop link) | HGLRC Hermes (`TLM2`) | $16 |\n| Battery (flight) | Upgrade Energy 6S3P 12 Ah Amprius (`BAT10`) | $275 |\n| Battery (dev ×2) | GNB 6S3P 12 Ah (`BAT22`) × 2 | $220 |\n| Video receiver | Skydroid 150CH 5.8 GHz UVC dual-antenna (`VRX6`) | $44 |\n| Ground antenna | TrueRC X-AIR 5.8 patch (`PATCH1`) | $37 |\n| Anti-spark filter | iFlight Anti Spark, XT60 (`ASF1`) | $15 |\n| Battery charger | HOTA D6 Pro (`CHG1`) | $112 |\n| USB-A→USB-C adapter | for the MacBook Air (USB-C only) | ~$11 |\n| FPV cam + VTX (air video) | bundled with the Chimera9 PNP | $0 |\n| GCS laptop | existing MacBook Air | $0 |\n| **Phase 1 subtotal** | | **~$1,355** |\n\n*See [`BOM.md`](BOM.md) for the full phased bill of materials (all 3 phases, sorted, with per-phase subtotals). Flight-controller firmware (ArduPilot/PX4 vs Betaflight) is a configuration choice, not a procured component — TBD.*\n\n## Support equipment (bench — reusable, not flown, not in system cost)\n**Battery charger — ✅ SELECTED: HOTA D6 Pro (`CHG1`), Phase 1** (now in the LOCKED table above). Formalized in the model as a `Charger` part def + `ChargerCandidates`, composed into `AerialThermalObservationSystem` as ground-support equipment. Requirement: 6S **balance** + **Li-ion *and* LiPo** modes + XT60, with enough power for the 12 Ah packs (Li-ion ≈ 0.5C → 6 A/~133 W; LiPo 1C → 12 A/~266 W). Alternatives considered:\n\n| Charger | ID | AC / DC power | Ch. | Notes | ~$ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **HOTA D6 Pro** ✅ **SELECTED** | `CHG1` | AC 200 W / DC 650 W · 15 A×2 | dual | community standard; Li-ion/LiPo/LiFe/LiHV, 1.6 A balance; best value | ~$112 |\n| ISDT 608AC | `CHG2` | AC/DC 200 W · 8 A | single | simplest; XT60 built-in; AC-integrated; great for a single pack | ~$75 |\n| ToolkitRC M6DAC | `CHG3` | AC 200 W / DC 700 W | dual | premium dual; full 700 W on DC | ~$120 |\n| HOTA S6 | `CHG4` | AC 400 W / DC 325 W×2 · 15 A×2 | dual | highest AC power → fastest 12 Ah charging | ~$140 |\n\nAll do 6S **Li-ion + LiPo** with balance and XT60 (lead). **Recommended: HOTA D6 Pro** (value + dual channel + AC convenience); step to the **HOTA S6** if you want ≥1C charging of the 12 Ah packs. *(Charging Li-ion: charge to 4.1–4.2 V/cell at ≤0.5C for long cell life; always balance-charge.)*\n\n## Not procured / external\n- **Viewing computer** — existing MacBook Air (external actor; excluded from cost).\n\n## Current reference build (full mission system)\n**Chimera9 ECO (AF3a PNP) + [battery TBD, leading BAT09] + T13 + SBC3** → ~58.6 min hover, ~$1,645 system (well under the $2,500 R4 cap), SBC fits the deck. See\n[`analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md`](analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md) /\n[`.csv`](analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.csv) for the full ranked loadouts.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783264569333}}
{"type":"message","id":"909c52c5","parentId":"2862b47c","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:16:21.933Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture. The user wants to:\n\n1. Move the SBC (SBC3) from Phase 3 to Phase 2\n2. Drop the DVR (DVR9) entirely since the SBC handles recording\n3. Update all documentation to reflect this\n4. Phase 3 becomes just \"SBC AI detection / autonomous route modification\" with no new procurement (since the SBC is already procured in Phase 2 now)\n\nLet me plan the changes:\n\n**BOM.md:**\n- Phase 2 → Remove DVR9 row, add SBC3 + SBC mount+cooling\n- Phase 3 → Remove SBC3 + mount (nothing left to procure? Or still keep the SBC mount+cooling there?)\n  Actually, Phase 3 is \"autonomous route modification\" — the SBC is the hardware but the software/configuration work is Phase 3. So we might keep an empty/informational Phase 3 or rename it to indicate it's a software/configuration phase.\n  \nActually, looking at the engineering plan more carefully:\n- Phase 2: thermal camera + onboard recording + OpenHD\n- Phase 3: On-board SBC detection + autonomous route modification\n\nThe SBC enables Phase 3, but the procurement of the SBC is in Phase 2 now. Phase 3 is about deployment, model training, configuration.\n\nLet me think about what makes sense:\n- **Phase 2** becomes: thermal camera + SBC procurement (recording via SBC) + OpenHD digital downlink\n- **Phase 3** becomes: AI detection model deployment + autonomous route modification (no new procurement since SBC was already bought)\n\nFor BOM.md: \n- Phase 2: Remove DVR9 (-$129), add SBC3 ($126) + mount ($15). Net change: -$129 + $141 = +$12\n- Phase 3: Empty procurement (or keep it as informational)\n\nWait, actually the Phase 3 already had $141 total. Let me re-calculate:\n\nCurrent Phase 2 subtotal: $924 (T13 $650 + DVR9 $129 + WLAN_AIR1 $20 + WLAN_GND1 $65 + ANT_GND1/2 $60 + VMware $0)\nNew Phase 2 subtotal: $924 - $129 (DVR9) + $126 (SBC3) + $15 (SBC mount) = $936\n\nCurrent Phase 3 subtotal: $141 (SBC3 $126 + mount $15)\nNew Phase 3 subtotal: $0 (nothing to procure)\n\nCurrent grand total: $2,419.75\nNew grand total: $2,419.75 - $129 = $2,290.75 (we dropped DVR9, added SBC3 which was already counted)\n\nWait no, let me be more careful. Currently:\n- Phase 1: $1,354.75\n- Phase 2: ~$924.00 (T13 $650 + DVR9 $129 + WLAN_AIR1 $20 + WLAN_GND1 $65 + ANT_GND1/2 $60 + VMware $0)\n- Phase 3: $141.00 (SBC3 $126 + mount $15)\n- Grand total: $2,419.75 (but is that ~$924 + $141? $1,354.75 + $924 + $141 = $2,419.75 ✓)\n\nAfter changes:\n- Phase 2: T13 $650 + WLAN_AIR1 $20 + WLAN_GND1 $65 + ANT_GND1/2 $60 + VMware $0 + SBC3 $126 + mount $15 = $936\n- Phase 3: $0 (software/configuration only)\n- Grand total: $1,354.75 + $936 + $0 = $2,290.75\n\nR4 system cost: $2,290.75 - $220 (dev batteries) - $112 (charger) = $1,958.75\n\nNow for systems_engineering_plan.md:\n- Phase 2: Replace DVR with SBC in new components and description\n- Phase 3: Update to say SBC was already procured, this phase is about AI deployment\n\nSELECTED_COMPONENTS.md:\n- Update open/in-progress table to reflect DVR is dropped, SBC moved to Phase 2\n\nLet me also check other files that reference the phase structure.\n\nOther files to check/update:\n- model.sysml — phase references? The model.sysml has doc comments referencing phases. Probably not worth updating those since they're architectural descriptions.\n- README.md — might reference phases\n- session-handoffs — historical, shouldn't change\n\nLet me also check:\n- analysis/flight_time_results.md — references Phase but that's about the sweep analysis, not procurement phases\n- CLAUDE.md — might reference DVR as Phase 1-2 part\n\nLet me start making all the edits.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me check a few more files that reference the phase structure and DVR.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_398f949336da4833b7825fb3","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rn \"DVR9\\|standalone DVR\\|DVR is\\|DVR no longer\\|Phase 2\\|Phase 3\" --include=\"*.md\" --include=\"*.sysml\" . | grep -v \"flight_time\\|\\.git\\|node_modules\\|analysis/\\|memory/\\|session-handoffs/\\|\\.sysml:\" | grep -i \"dvr\\|phase\" | head -30"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rn \\\"DVR9\\\\|standalone DVR\\\\|DVR is\\\\|DVR no longer\\\\|Phase 2\\\\|Phase 3\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.sysml\\\" . | grep -v \\\"flight_time\\\\|\\\\.git\\\\|node_modules\\\\|analysis/\\\\|memory/\\\\|session-handoffs/\\\\|\\\\.sysml:\\\" | grep -i \\\"dvr\\\\|phase\\\" | head -30\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e951b71ff78c437fa511f19b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rn \"DVR\\|DVR9\" --include=\"*.md\" . | grep -v \"\\.git\\|node_modules\\|session-handoffs\\|memory/\" | head -30"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && grep -rn \\\"DVR\\\\|DVR9\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" . | grep -v \\\"\\\\.git\\\\|node_modules\\\\|session-handoffs\\\\|memory/\\\" | head -30\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":23315,"output":1315,"cacheRead":20480,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":1059,"totalTokens":45110,"cost":{"input":0.0023315,"output":0.000263,"cacheRead":0.0004096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0030040999999999996}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783264569336,"responseId":"gen-1783264569-fTQ9ZLRt25r0JL4iqUnE"}}
{"type":"message","id":"03f03678","parentId":"909c52c5","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:16:21.970Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_398f949336da4833b7825fb3","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"./MODEL_ISSUES.md:139:   (Mission Planner / QGroundControl tuning profiles) and the Phase 3 SBC MAVLink\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:284:        DVR is dropped (initially CVBS-only; relaxed in **C12** with digital DVRs).\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:301:      DVR9, so **14 of 16 thermals are now viable**. Only T7 (raw SPI) and T16 (raw\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:305:      stage build (Phase 4: SBC present, no DVR). Per the staged plan the DVR is\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:335:      laptop is the ground station. **PRIMARY (Phase 2+):** an ELRS USB dongle\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:472:    - **Phase restructure (4 → 3):** merged old Phase 1 (basic flight) + Phase 2\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:474:      dongle into Phase 1**. Old Phase 3 (thermal + DVR) → **Phase 2**; old Phase 4\n./MODEL_ISSUES.md:475:      (SBC) → **Phase 3**. The DVR is now a Phase 1–2 part; the SBC records at Phase 3.\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:4:the old Phase 1 \"basic flight\" and Phase 2 \"FPV + waypoints\" are now a single Phase 1).\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:45:## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + Onboard Recording\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:50:- ThermalVideoRecorder — **Monster UVC Recorder** (`DVR9`, standalone USB-UVC DVR to microSD)\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:65:## Phase 3 — On-Board Detection + Autonomous Route Modification\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:68:**New Components (vs Phase 2)**\n./systems_engineering_plan.md:72:**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 2, plus the SBC (the SBC records at this stage, so the DVR is no longer required).\n./REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md:51:2. **Phase 2 — Thermal + recording:** adds the thermal camera + onboard DVR (footage survives RF loss).\n./REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md:52:3. **Phase 3 — Onboard autonomy:** adds the SBC for live detection/classification + autonomous route modification (MAVLink). *The DVR is a Phase 1–2 part; at Phase 3 the SBC records.*\n./REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md:140:- **Reliability:** control and video links reliable to ≥ 2.8 km LOS (**R4_GCS_RANGE**); footage retained on-card independent of RF link quality (Phase 3 DVR).\n./CLAUDE.md:46:- **Onboard thermal recording** via an inline DVR (`ThermalVideoRecorder`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. CVBS DVRs (DVR1-6, CVBS-in → microSD → pass-through to VTX) cover analog thermals; digital DVRs (DVR7-9: HDMI/USB-UVC) cover digital-output thermals. The DVR is an **earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part only** — at the SBC stage (Phase 3) the SBC records, so the DVR is excluded from max-flight-time but retained for camera↔DVR compatibility and cost.\n./CLAUDE.md:50:Defines three incremental phases (merged from the original four — old Phase 1 basic flight + Phase 2 FPV/waypoints are now one Phase 1), each listing the requirements satisfied, components required, and concrete build steps:\n./CLAUDE.md:65:**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and **V2** thermal↔DVR (a thermal no DVR can record — raw SPI/CMOS — is dropped). The **DVR is not crossed and is excluded from flight time**: it is an earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part, so the headline endurance is the SBC-stage build (SBC present, DVR removed); the DVR is kept only for earlier-stage camera↔DVR compatibility and for cost. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro). **Recommended baseline:** DarwinFPV 129 (AF9a) + 4S 12Ah Amprius + T13 + SBC3 → 69.1 min hover, ~$1,505 system (well under the $2,500 R4 cap). (The earlier KOLAS7 \"71 min winner\" was a data artifact — its modeled mass omitted the 188 g of motors; corrected to as-built ~540–565 g, see `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §D.) See also `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C11-C12.\n./SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md:34:| **Video receiver (VRX)** | **Skydroid 150CH 5.8 GHz true-diversity UVC** | `VRX6` | 2026-06-30 | sweep (matched VRX, CVBS) | laptop-direct UVC (QuickTime/OBS on macOS); receives the bundled analog VTX (pulled forward from Phase 2). | **1** |\n./SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md:65:| **On-board DVR** | open (**Phase 2**) | `DVR9` (rep.) | **Phase 1–2 only** — at the SBC stage (**Phase 3**) the SBC records; the DVR is costed/compatibility-checked but not in the SBC-stage flight-time. |\n./README.md:94:- **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count, **V2** thermal↔DVR video format. The DVR is excluded from max-flight-time (it's a Phase 1–2 part; the SBC records at Phase 3) but kept for earlier-stage compatibility + cost.\n./INTERFACE_REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md:104:- **Priority:** High (Phase 3). **Type:** Real-time video stream.\n./INTERFACE_REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md:119:- **Priority:** High (Phase 2). **Type:** Real-time video stream.\n./INTERFACE_REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md:126:- **Priority:** Medium (Phase 3). **Type:** Real-time video stream (pass-through).\n./BOM.md:7:flight + Phase 2 FPV/waypoints are now a single Phase 1).\n./BOM.md:36:## Phase 2 — EO/IR therma