{"type":"message","id":"aeefb847","parentId":"be30a8d0","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:18:52.165Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dd805b60290d44409c3e194f","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"9:- **34 real configurations** = airframe × battery × VTX, fully crossed (respecting airframe component inclusion) and **filtered for interface compatibility**; thermal fixed to **T13** and SBC fixed to **SBC3** (design choices, not swept). The DVR is compatibility-gated, not crossed, and excluded from flight time (it is an earlier-stage part; the SBC records at the SBC stage).\n13:- **Cost (R4 ≤ $2,500):** each config's drone cost + a laptop-based GCS = control base **$126** (Phase-1/backup handheld radio + ELRS USB control dongle) **plus a ground video receiver matched to the airframe's VTX format** (CVBS Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver $45; DJI DJI Goggles N3 $230; WALKSNAIL Walksnail Avatar HD Goggles L $199). Analog frames use the cheap analog VRX; frames with a digital air unit (DJI/Walksnail) carry the matching goggles. Bundled VTX/FPV/GPS/RX add $0 (already in the airframe price); the DVR is included (earlier-stage part).\n14:- **Compatibility filtering** (declared in `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::Compatibility`): 46 raw pairings reduced to 34 real configs — pruned 12 on battery↔airframe cell-count (P1, e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and 0 on thermal↔DVR video format (V2, a thermal whose output no DVR can record — CVBS via DVR1-6 or digital HDMI/USB via DVR7-9)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":27,"aggregated":"9:- **34 real configurations** = airframe × battery × VTX, fully crossed (respecting airframe component inclusion) and **filtered for interface compatibility**; thermal fixed to **T13** and SBC fixed to **SBC3** (design choices, not swept). The DVR is compatibility-gated, not crossed, and excluded from flight time (it is an earlier-stage part; the SBC records at the SBC stage).\n13:- **Cost (R4 ≤ $2,500):** each config's drone cost + a laptop-based GCS = control base **$126** (Phase-1/backup handheld radio + ELRS USB control dongle) **plus a ground video receiver matched to the airframe's VTX format** (CVBS Skydroid 150CH 5.8GHz True-Diversity UVC Receiver $45; DJI DJI Goggles N3 $230; WALKSNAIL Walksnail Avatar HD Goggles L $199). Analog frames use the cheap analog VRX; frames with a digital air unit (DJI/Walksnail) carry the matching goggles. Bundled VTX/FPV/GPS/RX add $0 (already in the airframe price); the DVR is included (earlier-stage part).\n14:- **Compatibility filtering** (declared in `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::Compatibility`): 46 raw pairings reduced to 34 real configs — pruned 12 on battery↔airframe cell-count (P1, e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and 0 on thermal↔DVR video format (V2, a thermal whose output no DVR can record — CVBS via DVR1-6 or digital HDMI/USB via DVR7-9).","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783264732164}}
{"type":"message","id":"2704df5e","parentId":"aeefb847","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:18:52.165Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9a4f3f50559b40629a97d63e","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"5:Ranked by **endurance-per-dollar** = max hover flight time (min) ÷ total system cost (USD) × 1000 — i.e. **minutes of hover per $1,000**. Only configs meeting R6 (≥ 30 min) and the thrust/feasibility check are ranked. Each entry lists the **complete system bill of materials** by actual product name. Peripherals shown as *included with airframe* are bundled in a BNF/PNP airframe (no separate part or cost); the DVR is an earlier-stage recorder (counted in cost, excluded from flight time).\n26:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n33:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n40:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n47:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":27,"aggregated":"5:Ranked by **endurance-per-dollar** = max hover flight time (min) ÷ total system cost (USD) × 1000 — i.e. **minutes of hover per $1,000**. Only configs meeting R6 (≥ 30 min) and the thrust/feasibility check are ranked. Each entry lists the **complete system bill of materials** by actual product name. Peripherals shown as *included with airframe* are bundled in a BNF/PNP airframe (no separate part or cost); the DVR is an earlier-stage recorder (counted in cost, excluded from flight time).\n26:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n33:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n40:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\n47:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783264732165}}
{"type":"message","id":"d4014f2a","parentId":"2704df5e","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:19:05.026Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a substantial change. The DVR is referenced across many files. But note that the policy in MEMORY.md says `model.sysml` cannot be modified without explicit approval. Let me proceed with the non-`model.sysml` files first and ask about `model.sysml`.\n\nAlso, `candidates.sysml` mentions DVR9 as a candidate part. We can remove it or just leave it as an unused candidate. Since the user wants the DVR \"completely removed from the architecture\", I should remove it from the selected parts but could leave it in candidates.sysml as an unused option (it's a data file). Let me think about what \"completely removed from the architecture\" means.\n\nAlso, the `model.sysml` has a `ThermalVideoRecorder` part def and a `recorder` part. Since the user is dropping the DVR entirely and using the SBC for recording, I should remove those too. But MEMORY.md requires explicit approval to modify `model.sysml`.\n\nLet me also check what CLAUDE.md says about DVR — it's a configuration guide.\n\nLet me handle all the files I can edit freely, and ask about model.sysml.\n\nActually, let me re-read the MEMORY.md policy:\n\n> **Policy Statement:**  \n> The Surveillance Drone SysML V2 model (`model.sysml`) is a critical engineering artifact that **cannot be modified, updated, moved, or removed** without **explicit prior approval** from the user (David Daniel).\n\nSo I need to ask about model.sysml. Let me present the full scope of changes needed, ask about model.sysml, and do all the free edits.\n\nLet me plan what needs to happen:\n\n**Files to edit (no approval needed):**\n\n1. **BOM.md**\n   - Remove DVR9 row from Phase 2 table\n   - Add SBC3 + mount to Phase 2\n   - Update Phase 2 subtitle: \"thermal camera + onboard recording + OpenHD\" → \"thermal camera + SBC recording + OpenHD\"\n   - Update Phase 2 subtotal\n   - Remove empty Phase 3 hardware procurement section (or move SBC section to Phase 2)\n   - Update totals\n   - Update next steps\n   - Remove reference to Phase 3 hardware procurement\n\n2. **systems_engineering_plan.md**\n   - Phase 2: Remove DVR references, add SBC references\n   - Phase 3: Remove SBC hardware procurement, make it pure software phase\n   - Update phase steps\n\n3. **SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md**\n   - Remove DVR row from open/table\n   - Add SBC to Phase 2 table\n   - Update phase descriptions\n\n4. **REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md**\n   - Update Phase 2 and Phase 3 descriptions\n\n5. **CLAUDE.md**\n   - Update DVR references\n\n6. **README.md**\n   - Update DVR references\n\n7. **analysis/flight_time_results.md**\n   - Update DVR references in text\n\n8. **analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md**\n   - Update \"DVR: Monster UVC Recorder\" → \"Recording: SBC3 (USB-UVC)\" or similar\n   - Update the top matter about the DVR\n\n9. **analysis/flight_time_instances.sysml**\n   - This is a generated output; removing DVR from the architecture would mean the instances should not reference DVR9. But this is analysis output data... Might need to leave as-is since it's historical.\n\n10. **analysis/market_analyses_and_research/thermal_dvr_market_analysis.md**\n    - This is research, not architecture; can leave as-is\n\n11. **MODEL_ISSUES.md**\n    - Update DVR decision records to reflect the change\n\n**Files needing approval:**\n12. **model.sysml** — Remove `ThermalVideoRecorder` part def and associated component\n\n13. **candidates.sysml** — Remove DVR9 candidate, or mark as historical. Actually, candidates.sysml is a database of candidates, it's fine to keep old candidates. But the user said \"completely removed from the architecture\" — so I should prune it from SELECTED_COMPONENTS.\n\nLet me be strategic here. I'll:\n1. Do all the documentation edits\n2. Ask about model.sysml\n3. Leave candidates.sysml as-is (it's a parts database, old candidates are fine to keep)\n4. Leave analysis files that are historical results\n\nActually, the flight_time_instances.sysml and flight_time_results.md/fight_time_value_ranking.md are _analysis outputs_ — they were generated based on the previous architecture. They represent historical analysis. I should update the explanatory text in the analysis docs (the narrative parts), but the instance data itself is historical.\n\nLet me proceed with all the documentation changes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"That's a lot of files. Let me scope the full impact, then ask about the one file that needs your approval before I touch it.\n\n**Free to edit (no approval needed):**\n- `BOM.md` — Phase 2 restructure\n- `systems_engineering_plan.md` — Phase descriptions and steps\n- `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md` — DVR row removal\n- `REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md` — Phase descriptions\n- `CLAUDE.md` — DVR references\n- `README.md` — DVR references\n- `MODEL_ISSUES.md` — decision records\n- `analysis/flight_time_results.md` — explanatory text\n- `analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md` — per-entry DVR lines\n\n**Needs your approval (per MEMORY.md policy):**\n- **`model.sysml`** — contains `part def ThermalVideoRecorder` (line 732) and a `recorder : ThermalVideoRecorder` part (line 962) that would need removal\n- **`candidates.sysml`** — contains `part DVR9` definition (line 3203); I'd just leave this as an unused historical candidate unless you want it pruned\n\n**Data files I'd leave as-is (historical analysis):**\n- `analysis/flight_time_instances.sysml` — auto-generated sweep output with `dvr = \"DVR9\"` references; these are historical run data\n- `analysis/market_analyses_and_research/thermal_dvr_market_analysis.md` — research doc, not architecture\n\n---\n\nBefore I start the batch edit — do I have your approval to remove the `ThermalVideoRecorder` part def and the associated `recorder` part from **`model.sysml`**?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","mo