II RHCP patch antenna | `PATCH1` | [truerc.com](https://truerc.com/63425-x-air-58-mk-ii-rp-sma) | $36.85 |$\n| iFlight Anti Spark Filter (XT60, 150 A) | `ASF1` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/index.php?route=product/product&product_id=3474) | $14.99 |$\n| HOTA D6 Pro battery charger | `CHG1` | [hotarc.com](https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0FLXL4SZW/ref=ox_sc_act_image_1?smid=A10OEFIP1P2D8&th=1) | $111.55 |$\n| USB-AM-bM-^FM-^RUSB-C adapter (MacBook Air) | M-bM-^@M-^T | generic | $11.00 |$\n| FPV camera + 5.8 GHz analog VTX | *(bundled w/ `AF3a`)* | M-bM-^@M-^T | $0.00 |$\n| GCS laptop (existing MacBook Air) | M-bM-^@M-^T | M-bM-^@M-^T | $0.00 |$\n| **Phase 1 subtotal** | | | **$1,354.75** |$\n$\n## Phase 2 M-bM-^@M-^T EO/IR thermal camera + onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink$\n$\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |$\n|---|---|---|--:|$\n| PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640M-CM-^W512, 12 M-BM-5m, 13 mm) | `T13` | [thermal-image.com](https://www.thermal-image.com/product/mini-640-uncooled-lwir-thermal-camera-module/) | $650.00 |$\n| Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) | `DVR9` | [amazon.com](https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Monster+UVC+Recorder) | $129.00 |$\n| LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 RTL8812EU bare WiFi module (air side) + USB-A stub + 2M-CM-^W u.flM-bM-^FM-^RRP-SMA pigtails | `WLAN_AIR1` | [aliexpress.com](https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005007098141054.html) | ~$20.00 |$\n| Alfa AWUS036ACH RTL8812AU USB-C WiFi adapter (ground side) | `WLAN_GND1` | [rokland.com](https://store.rokland.com/products/alfa-awus036ach-usb-c-802-11ac-ac1200-dual-band-high-power-wifi-usb-adapter) | $65.00 |$\n| Foxeer Echo 2 Max 5.8 GHz linear patch antenna M-CM-^W 2 (ground diversity, 60M-BM-0 beam, RP-SMA male) | `ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2` | [foxeer.com](https://www.foxeer.com/foxeer-echo-2-max-high-gain-antenna-g-434) | $60.00 |$\n| VMware Fusion (ground station VM M-bM-^@M-^T free personal use) | M-bM-^@M-^T | vmware.com | $0.00 |$\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$924.00** |$\n$\n## Phase 3 M-bM-^@M-^T On-board SBC detection + autonomous route modification$\n$\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |$\n|---|---|---|--:|$\n| NanoPi M5, 4 GB SBC (Rockchip RK3576) | `SBC3` | [friendlyelec.com](https://www.friendlyelec.com/index.php?route=product/product&path=69&product_id=309) | $126.00 |$\n| SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + 30 mm fan + heat-set hardware) | M-bM-^@M-^T | fabricated ([reference/cad-resources.md](reference/cad-resources.md)) | ~$15.00 |$\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$141.00** |$\n$\n---$\n$\n## Totals$\n$\n| Phase | Subtotal |$\n|---|--:|$\n| Phase 1 M-bM-^@M-^T flight + FPV + waypoints | $1,354.75 |$\n| Phase 2 M-bM-^@M-^T thermal + recording + OpenHD digital downlink | ~$924.00 |$\n| Phase 3 M-bM-^@M-^T SBC autonomy | $141.00 |$\n| **Grand total (all procurement)** | **~$2,419.75** |$\n$\n**R4 integrated-system cost M-bM-^IM-^H $2,088** (M-bM-^IM-$ $2,500 M-bM-^\\M-^S) M-bM-^@M-^T the grand total minus **reusable/support$\nitems not part of the per-drone flight system**: the 2M-CM-^W `BAT22` development packs ($220) and$\nthe `CHG1` charger ($100). Both totals are under the $2,500 R4 cap.$\n$","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265123513}}
{"type":"message","id":"03a21df7","parentId":"2662c31d","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:25:47.034Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file uses UTF-8 em dashes (—) which are multibyte characters. Let me rewrite the BOM.md file entirely since the em dashes and special characters are making the exact match tricky. I'll use the write tool to do a complete rewrite of the BOM.md.\n\nActually, let me try using exec with sed or a Python script to do the replacement, since the edit tool is having trouble with the special characters. Or I can just use write to completely rewrite the BOM.md file.\n\nLet me just rewrite BOM.md wholesale, it'll be cleaner.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"The em dashes and special characters are making exact matching tricky. I'll rewrite `BOM.md` entirely since it's the cleanest approach.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1feb4dc435ec4b9a80ff4359","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md","content":"# Bill of Materials (BOM) — Thermal Surveillance Drone\n\nFull procurement list, **sorted by build phase** with a subtotal per phase. Derived from\n[`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md) (selections) and\n[`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml) (names, IDs, links, costs). **Part #** = the model\ncandidate ID (the project's internal part number). Three phases.\n\n> **Flight battery = `BAT10`** (Upgrade Energy 6S 12 Ah Amprius) — `BAT09` is out of stock.\n> **2× `BAT22`** (GNB) are procured as development/shakedown packs (spare the Amprius on early flights).\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 — Basic flight + FPV downlink + waypoints\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| iFlight Chimera9 ECO 6S (9\", PNP) + **GPS pre-installed** | `AF3a` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/Chimera9-ECO-6S-Pro2068) | $457.99 |\n| HQ 9X4X3 props — 4-pack (extra set) | — | shop.iflight.com / HQ | $17.00 |\n| iFlight True Diversity ELRS receiver | `iFlightTD` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/) | $31.99 |\n| RadioMaster TX12 Mark II ELRS radio | `TX5` | [radiomasterrc.com](https://www.radiomasterrc.com/products/tx12) | $117.93 |\n| HGLRC Hermes ELRS SIM USB Dongle — primary laptop control + telemetry | `TLM2` | [amazon.com](https://www.amazon.com/s?k=HGLRC+Hermes+ELRS+USB+dongle) | $16.00 |\n| Battery **(flight)** — Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S3P 12 Ah Amprius | `BAT10` | [upgrade-energy.com](https://www.upgrade-energy.com/) | $275.00 |\n| Battery **(development, ×2)** — GNB 6S3P 12 Ah 21700 Li-ion | `BAT22` | [gaoneng.shop](https://www.gaoneng.shop/products/gaoneng-gnb-6s-22.2v-12000mah-10c-xt60-li-ion-battery-made-with-li-ion-lithium-ion-21700) | $220.00 |\n| Skydroid 5.8 GHz 150CH UVC receiver (**dual antenna**) | `VRX6` | [alibaba.com](https://www.alibaba.com/product-detail/SKYDROID-5-8GHz-FPV-Receiver-UVC_1601393061166.html) *(select dual-antenna variant; confirm price at checkout)* | ~$44.45 |\n| TrueRC X-AIR 5.8 MK II RHCP patch antenna | `PATCH1` | [truerc.com](https://truerc.com/63425-x-air-58-mk-ii-rp-sma) | $36.85 |\n| iFlight Anti Spark Filter (XT60, 150 A) | `ASF1` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/index.php?route=product/product&product_id=3474) | $14.99 |\n| HOTA D6 Pro battery charger | `CHG1` | [hotarc.com](https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0FLXL4SZW/ref=ox_sc_act_image_1?smid=A10OEFIP1P2D8&th=1) | $111.55 |\n| USB-A→USB-C adapter (MacBook Air) | — | generic | $11.00 |\n| FPV camera + 5.8 GHz analog VTX | *(bundled w/ `AF3a`)* | — | $0.00 |\n| GCS laptop (existing MacBook Air) | — | — | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 1 subtotal** | | | **$1,354.75** |\n\n## Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm) | `T13` | [thermal-image.com](https://www.thermal-image.com/product/mini-640-uncooled-lwir-thermal-camera-module/) | $650.00 |\n| NanoPi M5, 4 GB SBC (Rockchip RK3576) — onboard recording + AI inference | `SBC3` | [friendlyelec.com](https://www.friendlyelec.com/index.php?route=product/product&path=69&product_id=309) | $126.00 |\n| SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + 30 mm fan + heat-set hardware) | — | fabricated ([reference/cad-resources.md](reference/cad-resources.md)) | ~$15.00 |\n| LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 RTL8812EU bare WiFi module (air side) + USB-A stub + 2× u.fl→RP-SMA pigtails | `WLAN_AIR1` | [aliexpress.com](https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005007098141054.html) | ~$20.00 |\n| Alfa AWUS036ACH RTL8812AU USB-C WiFi adapter (ground side) | `WLAN_GND1` | [rokland.com](https://store.rokland.com/products/alfa-awus036ach-usb-c-802-11ac-ac1200-dual-band-high-power-wifi-usb-adapter) | $65.00 |\n| Foxeer Echo 2 Max 5.8 GHz linear patch antenna × 2 (ground diversity, 60° beam, RP-SMA male) | `ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2` | [foxeer.com](https://www.foxeer.com/foxeer-echo-2-max-high-gain-antenna-g-434) | $60.00 |\n| VMware Fusion (ground station VM — free personal use) | — | vmware.com | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$936.00** |\n\n## Phase 3 — AI detection + autonomous route modification (software)\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| All hardware on-board since Phase 2. Phase 3 is software-only: deploy INT8-quantized model via RKNN toolchain, integrate MAVLink autonomous route modification. | — | — | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$0.00** |\n\n---\n\n## Totals\n\n| Phase | Subtotal |\n|---|---|\n| Phase 1 — flight + FPV + waypoints | $1,354.75 |\n| Phase 2 — thermal + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink | ~$936.00 |\n| Phase 3 — AI deployment (software only) | $0.00 |\n| **Grand total (all procurement)** | **~$2,290.75** |\n\n**R4 integrated-system cost ≈ $1,960** (≤ $2,500 ✓) — the grand total minus **reusable/support\nitems not part of the per-drone flight system**: the 2× `BAT22` development packs ($220) and\nthe `CHG1` charger ($100). Both totals are under the $2,500 R4 cap.\n\n## Next steps\n- **Phase 2 pricing** — T13 updated to $650.00 ($590 base + $60 shipping, confirmed 2026-07-05).\n  DVR9 removed from architecture — SBC handles onboard recording (moved from Phase 3).\n  Remaining items: confirm actual purchase prices for WLAN_AIR1, WLAN_GND1, and Foxeer Echo 2 Max\n  antennas; update candidates.sysml cost_USD and BOM subtotal accordingly.\n- **Phase 3 pricing** — all hardware procured in Phase 2; Phase 3 is software-only (RKNN model\n  deployment, MAVLink integration), $0 hardware.\n- Recompute grand total and R4 system cost once remaining Phase 2 prices are confirmed.\n\n## Notes\n- **Part # = model candidate ID** (the internal part number in [`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml));\n  \"—\" = no catalog part yet (generic/fabricated/TBD).\n- **Battery:** `BAT10` is the flight default (`BAT09` out of stock); the **2× `BAT22`** are\n  development/shakedown packs (cheap, robust — fly these first, spare the Amprius).\n- **Bundled at $0:** the FPV camera + analog VTX ship with the Chimera9 ECO PNP. **GPS is now\n  pre-installed** (iFlight BLITZ M10 GPS V2 Mini, `G4`; cost folded into the airframe line at\n  $457.99 incl. shipping). **Existing at $0:** the MacBook Air GCS.\n- **DVR removed:** the standalone Monster UVC Recorder (`DVR9`) was dropped from the architecture\n  (2026-07-05). The SBC (`SBC3`) handles all onboard recording via USB-UVC from the T13 thermal\n  camera, eliminating the need for a separate DVR.\n- **TBD lines:** the flight-controller firmware (ArduPilot/PX4 vs Betaflight — a configuration\n  choice, no cost).\n- The flight-time sweep reports ~$1,690 for the drone + GCS using *cost-representative* RX/radio;\n  this BOM uses the **actual selected** parts (iFlight TD RX + TX12 MkII radio) plus GPS, dongle,\n  charger, adapter, dev batteries, and the SBC mount — hence the higher, complete figure."},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md\", \"content\": \"# Bill of Materials (BOM) — Thermal Surveillance Drone\\n\\nFull procurement list, **sorted by build phase** with a subtotal per phase. Derived from\\n[`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md) (selections) and\\n[`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml) (names, IDs, links, costs). **Part #** = the model\\ncandidate ID (the project's internal part number). Three phases.\\n\\n> **Flight battery = `BAT10`** (Upgrade Energy 6S 12 Ah Amprius) — `BAT09` is out of stock.\\n> **2× `BAT22`** (GNB) are procured as development/shakedown packs (spare the Amprius on early flights).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1 — Basic flight + FPV downlink + waypoints\\n\\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| iFlight Chimera9 ECO 6S (9\\\", PNP) + **GPS pre-installed** | `AF3a` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/Chimera9-ECO-6S-Pro2068) | $457.99 |\\n| HQ 9X4X3 props — 4-pack (extra set) | — | shop.iflight.com / HQ | $17.00 |\\n| iFlight True Diversity ELRS receiver | `iFlightTD` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/) | $31.99 |\\n| RadioMaster TX12 Mark II ELRS radio | `TX5` | [radiomasterrc.com](https://www.radiomasterrc.com/products/tx12) | $117.93 |\\n| HGLRC Hermes ELRS SIM USB Dongle — primary laptop control + telemetry | `TLM2` | [amazon.com](https://www.amazon.com/s?k=HGLRC+Hermes+ELRS+USB+dongle) | $16.00 |\\n| Battery **(flight)** — Upgrade Energy GREEN V2 6S3P 12 Ah Amprius | `BAT10` | [upgrade-energy.com](https://www.upgrade-energy.com/) | $275.00 |\\n| Battery **(development, ×2)** — GNB 6S3P 12 Ah 21700 Li-ion | `BAT22` | [gaoneng.shop](https://www.gaoneng.shop/products/gaoneng-gnb-6s-22.2v-12000mah-10c-xt60-li-ion-battery-made-with-li-ion-lithium-ion-21700) | $220.00 |\\n| Skydroid 5.8 GHz 150CH UVC receiver (**dual antenna**) | `VRX6` | [alibaba.com](https://www.alibaba.com/product-detail/SKYDROID-5-8GHz-FPV-Receiver-UVC_1601393061166.html) *(select dual-antenna variant; confirm price at checkout)* | ~$44.45 |\\n| TrueRC X-AIR 5.8 MK II RHCP patch antenna | `PATCH1` | [truerc.com](https://truerc.com/63425-x-air-58-mk-ii-rp-sma) | $36.85 |\\n| iFlight Anti Spark Filter (XT60, 150 A) | `ASF1` | [shop.iflight.com](https://shop.iflight.com/index.php?route=product/product&product_id=3474) | $14.99 |\\n| HOTA D6 Pro battery charger | `CHG1` | [hotarc.com](https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0FLXL4SZW/ref=ox_sc_act_image_1?smid=A10OEFIP1P2D8&th=1) | $111.55 |\\n| USB-A→USB-C adapter (MacBook Air) | — | generic | $11.00 |\\n| FPV camera + 5.8 GHz analog VTX | *(bundled w/ `AF3a`)* | — | $0.00 |\\n| GCS laptop (existing MacBook Air) | — | — | $0.00 |\\n| **Phase 1 subtotal** | | | **$1,354.75** |\\n\\n## Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink\\n\\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm) | `T13` | [thermal-image.com](https://www.thermal-image.com/product/mini-640-uncooled-lwir-thermal-camera-module/) | $650.00 |\\n| NanoPi M5, 4 GB SBC (Rockchip RK3576) — onboard recording + AI inference | `SBC3` | [friendlyelec.com](https://www.friendlyelec.com/index.php?route=product/product&path=69&product_id=309) | $126.00 |\\n| SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + 30 mm fan + heat-set hardware) | — | fabricated ([reference/cad-resources.md](reference/cad-resources.md)) | ~$15.00 |\\n| LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 RTL8812EU bare WiFi module (air side) + USB-A stub + 2× u.fl→RP-SMA pigtails | `WLAN_AIR1` | [aliexpress.com](https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005007098141054.html) | ~$20.00 |\\n| Alfa AWUS036ACH RTL8812AU USB-C WiFi adapter (ground side) | `WLAN_GND1` | [rokland.com](https://store.rokland.com/products/alfa-awus036ach-usb-c-802-11ac-ac1200-dual-band-high-power-wifi-usb-adapter) | $65.00 |\\n| Foxeer Echo 2 Max 5.8 GHz linear patch antenna × 2 (ground diversity, 60° beam, RP-SMA male) | `ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2` | [foxeer.com](https://www.foxeer.com/foxeer-echo-2-max-high-gain-antenna-g-434) | $60.00 |\\n| VMware Fusion (ground station VM — free personal use) | — | vmware.com | $0.00 |\\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$936.00** |\\n\\n## Phase 3 — AI detection + autonomous route modification (software)\\n\\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| All hardware on-board since Phase 2. Phase 3 is software-only: deploy INT8-quantized model via RKNN toolchain, integrate MAVLink autonomous route modification. | — | — | $0.00 |\\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$0.00** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Totals\\n\\n| Phase | Subtotal |\\n|---|---|\\n| Phase 1 — flight + FPV + waypoints | $1,354.75 |\\n| Phase 2 — thermal + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink | ~$936.00 |\\n| Phase 3 — AI deployment (software only) | $0.00 |\\n| **Grand total (all procurement)** | **~$2,290.75** |\\n\\n**R4 integrated-system cost ≈ $1,960** (≤ $2,500 ✓) — the grand total minus **reusable/support\\nitems not part of the per-drone flight system**: the 2× `BAT22` development packs ($220) and\\nthe `CHG1` charger ($100). Both totals are under the $2,500 R4 cap.\\n\\n## Next steps\\n- **Phase 2 pricing** — T13 updated to $650.00 ($590 base + $60 shipping, confirmed 2026-07-05).\\n  DVR9 removed from architecture — SBC handles onboard recording (moved from Phase 3).\\n  Remaining items: confirm actual purchase prices for WLAN_AIR1, WLAN_GND1, and Foxeer Echo 2 Max\\n  antennas; update candidates.sysml cost_USD and BOM subtotal accordingly.\\n- **Phase 3 pricing** — all hardware procured in Phase 2; Phase 3 is software-only (RKNN model\\n  deployment, MAVLink integration), $0 hardware.\\n- Recompute grand total and R4 system cost once remaining Phase 2 prices are confirmed.\\n\\n## Notes\\n- **Part # = model candidate ID** (the internal part number in [`candidates.sysml`](candidates.sysml));\\n  \\\"—\\\" = no catalog part yet (generic/fabricated/TBD).\\n- **Battery:** `BAT10` is the flight default (`BAT09` out of stock); the **2× `BAT22`** are\\n  development/shakedown packs (cheap, robust — fly these first, spare the Amprius).\\n- **Bundled at $0:** the FPV camera + analog VTX ship with the Chimera9 ECO PNP. **GPS is now\\n  pre-installed** (iFlight BLITZ M10 GPS V2 Mini, `G4`; cost folded into the airframe line at\\n  $457.99 incl. shipping). **Existing at $0:** the MacBook Air GCS.\\n- **DVR removed:** the standalone Monster UVC Recorder (`DVR9`) was dropped from the architecture\\n  (2026-07-05). The SBC (`SBC3`) handles all onboard recording via USB-UVC from the T13 thermal\\n  camera, eliminating the need for a separate DVR.\\n- **TBD lines:** the flight-controller firmware (ArduPilot/PX4 vs Betaflight — a configuration\\n  choice, no cost).\\n- The flight-time sweep reports ~$1,690 for the drone + GCS using *cost-representative* RX/radio;\\n  this BOM uses the **actual selected** parts (iFlight TD RX + TX12 MkII radio) plus GPS, dongle,\\n  charger, adapter, dev batteries, and the SBC mount — hence the higher, complete figure.\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":65376,"output":2466,"cacheRead":8192,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":119,"totalTokens":76034,"cost":{"input":0.006537599999999999,"output":0.0004932,"cacheRead":0.00016384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0071946399999999995}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783265123517,"responseId":"gen-1783265123-N0lNKUhQcJ9qqG7XBFGl"}}
{"type":"message","id":"cc22eeb2","parentId":"03a21df7","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:25:47.058Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1feb4dc435ec4b9a80ff4359","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 6748 bytes to /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265147058}}
{"type":"message","id":"18c4b0ca","parentId":"cc22eeb2","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:26:15.950Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me update the remaining files. Let me do the systems_engineering_plan.md, SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md, REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md, analysis/flight_time_results.md, analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md, README.md, CLAUDE.md, and MODEL_ISSUES.md.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Now the remaining files. Let me batch them efficiently"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0f65c1fce6574f89bb60622e","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"oldText":"## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + Onboard Recording\n**Goal** — Mount the thermal camera, record onboard to microSD, and downlink live thermal video.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\n- Thermal Camera Subsystem — **PurpleRiver Mini 640** (`T13`, 640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm lens, USB)\n- ThermalVideoRecorder — **Monster UVC Recorder** (`DVR9`, standalone USB-UVC DVR to microSD)\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera and DVR.\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Mount the thermal camera on the airframe (clear FOV, nose/chin) and power from the airframe rail.\n2. Route the thermal video → DVR (records to microSD) and to the laptop (live view).\n3. Configure the DVR to auto-start recording on power-up (per-flight files).\n4. Fly and recover thermal footage from microSD post-flight (footage survives RF loss).\n5. Confirm live thermal downlink on the laptop and Johnson detect/recognize performance at 90–120 m.\n\n**Result** — Thermal video recorded onboard (survives signal loss) with live downlink; meets the R3 detection/recognition requirements.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — On-Board Detection + Autonomous Route Modification\n**Goal** — Add on-board AI thermal detection/classification and dynamic mission adaptation.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 2)**\n- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU)\n- SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + fan — see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md))\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 2, plus the SBC (the SBC records at this stage, so the DVR is no longer required).\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Mount the SBC on a 3D-printed deck; connect to the airframe rail and the flight controller (UART/MAVLink).\n2. Route the thermal camera video → SBC (USB-UVC).\n3. Deploy the INT8-quantized detection/classification model via the RKNN toolchain (RKNPU2); verify ≥ ~25 fps.\n4. Map detections to MAVLink commands (loiter/adjust on a target); modify the mission in-flight.\n5. Validate fallback: if the SBC fails, the drone completes the current waypoint and RTLs.\n\n**Result** — Autonomous drone that detects and reacts to thermal targets, meeting all SBC and camera requirements.","newText":"## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + SBC Onboard Recording + OpenHD Digital Downlink\n**Goal** — Mount the thermal camera and SBC, record onboard via SBC, and downlink live thermal video via OpenHD.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\n- Thermal Camera Subsystem — **PurpleRiver Mini 640** (`T13`, 640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm lens, USB)\n- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU) — handles onboard recording + future AI inference\n- SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + fan — see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md))\n- WiFi adapter (air) — LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 (`WLAN_AIR1`) for OpenHD digital downlink\n- WiFi adapter (ground) — Alfa AWUS036ACH (`WLAN_GND1`) for OpenHD reception\n- Ground diversity antennas — Foxeer Echo 2 Max × 2 (`ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2`)\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera, SBC (with mount/cooling), and OpenHD digital downlink hardware.\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Mount the thermal camera on the airframe (clear FOV, nose/chin) and power from the airframe rail.\n2. Mount the SBC on a 3D-printed deck; connect to the airframe rail and the flight controller (UART/MAVLink).\n3. Route the thermal camera video → SBC (USB-UVC for recording + future inference).\n4. Configure the SBC to record thermal footage to onboard storage (microSD/eMMC) on power-up.\n5. Configure OpenHD digital downlink: SBC encodes H.264 → WiFi air module transmits WFB-ng protocol → ground WiFi adapter + Foxeer antennas receive on laptop VM.\n6. Fly and recover thermal footage from SBC post-flight (footage survives RF loss).\n7. Confirm live thermal downlink on the laptop and Johnson detect/recognize performance at 90–120 m.\n\n**Result** — Thermal video recorded onboard via SBC (survives signal loss) with OpenHD digital downlink; meets the R3 detection/recognition requirements. No separate DVR required.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — AI Detection + Autonomous Route Modification (Software)\n**Goal** — Deploy on-board AI thermal detection/classification and dynamic mission adaptation using the SBC already on-board.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 2)** — None (all hardware on-board since Phase 2).\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — same as Phase 2 (hardware).\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Deploy the INT8-quantized detection/classification model via the RKNN toolchain (RKNPU2); verify ≥ ~25 fps.\n2. Map detections to MAVLink commands (loiter/adjust on a target); modify the mission in-flight.\n3. Validate fallback: if the SBC fails, the drone completes the current waypoint and RTLs.\n\n**Result** — Autonomous drone that detects and reacts to thermal targets, meeting all SBC and camera requirements."}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/systems_engineering_plan.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"oldText\": \"## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + Onboard Recording\\n**Goal** — Mount the thermal camera, record onboard to microSD, and downlink live thermal video.\\n\\n**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\\n- Thermal Camera Subsystem — **PurpleRiver Mini 640** (`T13`, 640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm lens, USB)\\n- ThermalVideoRecorder — **Monster UVC Recorder** (`DVR9`, standalone USB-UVC DVR to microSD)\\n\\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera and DVR.\\n\\n**Phase Steps**\\n1. Mount the thermal camera on the airframe (clear FOV, nose/chin) and power from the airframe rail.\\n2. Route the thermal video → DVR (records to microSD) and to the laptop (live view).\\n3. Configure the DVR to auto-start recording on power-up (per-flight files).\\n4. Fly and recover thermal footage from microSD post-flight (footage survives RF loss).\\n5. Confirm live thermal downlink on the laptop and Johnson detect/recognize performance at 90–120 m.\\n\\n**Result** — Thermal video recorded onboard (survives signal loss) with live downlink; meets the R3 detection/recognition requirements.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 3 — On-Board Detection + Autonomous Route Modification\\n**Goal** — Add on-board AI thermal detection/classification and dynamic mission adaptation.\\n\\n**New Components (vs Phase 2)**\\n- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU)\\n- SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + fan — see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md))\\n\\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 2, plus the SBC (the SBC records at this stage, so the DVR is no longer required).\\n\\n**Phase Steps**\\n1. Mount the SBC on a 3D-printed deck; connect to the airframe rail and the flight controller (UART/MAVLink).\\n2. Route the thermal camera video → SBC (USB-UVC).\\n3. Deploy the INT8-quantized detection/classification model via the RKNN toolchain (RKNPU2); verify ≥ ~25 fps.\\n4. Map detections to MAVLink commands (loiter/adjust on a target); modify the mission in-flight.\\n5. Validate fallback: if the SBC fails, the drone completes the current waypoint and RTLs.\\n\\n**Result** — Autonomous drone that detects and reacts to thermal targets, meeting all SBC and camera requirements.\", \"newText\": \"## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + SBC Onboard Recording + OpenHD Digital Downlink\\n**Goal** — Mount the thermal camera and SBC, record onboard via SBC, and downlink live thermal video via OpenHD.\\n\\n**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\\n- Thermal Camera Subsystem — **PurpleRiver Mini 640** (`T13`, 640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm lens, USB)\\n- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU) — handles onboard recording + future AI inference\\n- SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + fan — see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md))\\n- WiFi adapter (air) — LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 (`WLAN_AIR1`) for OpenHD digital downlink\\n- WiFi adapter (ground) — Alfa AWUS036ACH (`WLAN_GND1`) for OpenHD reception\\n- Ground diversity antennas — Foxeer Echo 2 Max × 2 (`ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2`)\\n\\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera, SBC (with mount/cooling), and OpenHD digital downlink hardware.\\n\\n**Phase Steps**\\n1. Mount the thermal camera on the airframe (clear FOV, nose/chin) and power from the airframe rail.\\n2. Mount the SBC on a 3D-printed deck; connect to the airframe rail and the flight controller (UART/MAVLink).\\n3. Route the thermal camera video → SBC (USB-UVC for recording + future inference).\\n4. Configure the SBC to record thermal footage to onboard storage (microSD/eMMC) on power-up.\\n5. Configure OpenHD digital downlink: SBC encodes H.264 → WiFi air module transmits WFB-ng protocol → ground WiFi adapter + Foxeer antennas receive on laptop VM.\\n6. Fly and recover thermal footage from SBC post-flight (footage survives RF loss).\\n7. Confirm live thermal downlink on the laptop and Johnson detect/recognize performance at 90–120 m.\\n\\n**Result** — Thermal video recorded onboard via SBC (survives signal loss) with OpenHD digital downlink; meets the R3 detection/recognition requirements. No separate DVR required.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 3 — AI Detection + Autonomous Route Modification (Software)\\n**Goal** — Deploy on-board AI thermal detection/classification and dynamic mission adaptation using the SBC already on-board.\\n\\n**New Components (vs Phase 2)** — None (all hardware on-board since Phase 2).\\n\\n**Components Required (full list)** — same as Phase 2 (hardware).\\n\\n**Phase Steps**\\n1. Deploy the INT8-quantized detection/classification model via the RKNN toolchain (RKNPU2); verify ≥ ~25 fps.\\n2. Map detections to MAVLink commands (loiter/adjust on a target); modify the mission in-flight.\\n3. Validate fallback: if the SBC fails, the drone completes the current waypoint and RTLs.\\n\\n**Result** — Autonomous drone that detects and reacts to thermal targets, meeting all SBC and camera requirements.\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/systems_engineering_plan.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4a096bc1b3ed462f8a519a3f","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"| **On-board recording** | **SBC does it** — NanoPi M5 (`SBC3`) records thermal footage via USB-UVC from the T13. No separate DVR needed. | `—` | 2026-07-05 | DVR9 removed; SBC moved to Phase 2 procurement | SBC handles recording + inference in a single device; eliminates DVR cost ($129) and mass. | **2** |","oldText":"| **On-board DVR** | open (**Phase 2**) | `DVR9` (rep.) | **Phase 1–2 only** — at the SBC stage (**Phase 3**) the SBC records; the DVR is costed/compatibility-checked but not in the SBC-stage flight-time. |"}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"| **On-board recording** | **SBC does it** — NanoPi M5 (`SBC3`) records thermal footage via USB-UVC from the T13. No separate DVR needed. | `—` | 2026-07-05 | DVR9 removed; SBC moved to Phase 2 procurement | SBC handles recording + inference in a single device; eliminates DVR cost ($129) and mass. | **2** |\", \"oldText\": \"| **On-board DVR** | open (**Phase 2**) | `DVR9` (rep.) | **Phase 1–2 only** — at the SBC stage (**Phase 3**) the SBC records; the DVR is costed/compatibility-checked but not in the SBC-stage flight-time. |\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2223e2cf2d054544973652fd","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"2. **Phase 2 — Thermal + SBC + OpenHD downlink:** adds the thermal camera + SBC (recording + future inference) + OpenHD digital video downlink (footage survives RF loss; SBC records locally).\n3. **Phase 3 — Onboard autonomy (software):** deploys the detection/classification model on the already-installed SBC + integrates MAVLink autonomous route modification. *No hardware procurement in Phase 3.*","oldText":"2. **Phase 2 — Thermal + recording:** adds the thermal camera + onboard DVR (footage survives RF loss).\n3. **Phase 3 — Onboard autonomy:** adds the SBC for live detection/classification + autonomous route modification (MAVLink). *The DVR is a Phase 1–2 part; at Phase 3 the SBC records.*"},{"newText":"Internal interfaces (battery↔airframe power, payload power rails, the camera→SBC/VTX","oldText":"Internal interfaces (battery↔airframe power, payload power rails, the camera→DVR/SBC/VTX"},{"newText":"footage retained on-card independent of RF link quality (Phase 2+ SBC onboard recording).","oldText":"footage retained on-card independent of RF link quality (Phase 3 DVR)."}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"2. **Phase 2 — Thermal + SBC + OpenHD downlink:** adds the thermal camera + SBC (recording + future inference) + OpenHD digital video downlink (footage survives RF loss; SBC records locally).\\n3. **Phase 3 — Onboard autonomy (software):** deploys the detection/classification model on the already-installed SBC + integrates MAVLink autonomous route modification. *No hardware procurement in Phase 3.*\", \"oldText\": \"2. **Phase 2 — Thermal + recording:** adds the thermal camera + onboard DVR (footage survives RF loss).\\n3. **Phase 3 — Onboard autonomy:** adds the SBC for live detection/classification + autonomous route modification (MAVLink). *The DVR is a Phase 1–2 part; at Phase 3 the SBC records.*\"}, {\"newText\": \"Internal interfaces (battery↔airframe power, payload power rails, the camera→SBC/VTX\", \"oldText\": \"Internal interfaces (battery↔airframe power, payload power rails, the camera→DVR/SBC/VTX\"}, {\"newText\": \"footage retained on-card independent of RF link quality (Phase 2+ SBC onboard recording).\", \"oldText\": \"footage retained on-card independent of RF link quality (Phase 3 DVR).\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c223e0dd4e6b437281c3617b","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"filtered for interface compatibility**; thermal fixed to **T13** and SBC fixed to **SBC3** (design choices, not swept). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles all onboard recording via USB-UVC.","oldText":"filtered for interface compatibility**; thermal fixed to **T13** and SBC fixed to **SBC3** (design choices, not swept). The DVR is compatibility-gated, not crossed, and excluded from flight time (it is an earlier-stage part; the SBC records at the SBC stage)."},{"newText":"14:- **Compatibility filtering** (declared in `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::Compatibility`): 46 raw pairings reduced to 34 real configs — pruned 12 on battery↔airframe cell-count (P1, e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and 0 on thermal↔DVR video format (V2, a thermal whose output no DVR can record — CVBS via DVR1-6 or digital HDMI/USB via DVR7-9, now moot since DVR removed from architecture).","oldText":"14:- **Compatibility filtering** (declared in `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::Compatibility`): 46 raw pairings reduced to 34 real configs — pruned 12 on battery↔airframe cell-count (P1, e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and 0 on thermal↔DVR video format (V2, a thermal whose output no DVR can record — CVBS via DVR1-6 or digital HDMI/USB via DVR7-9)."}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/analysis/flight_time_results.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"filtered for interface compatibility**; thermal fixed to **T13** and SBC fixed to **SBC3** (design choices, not swept). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles all onboard recording via USB-UVC.\", \"oldText\": \"filtered for interface compatibility**; thermal fixed to **T13** and SBC fixed to **SBC3** (design choices, not swept). The DVR is compatibility-gated, not crossed, and excluded from flight time (it is an earlier-stage part; the SBC records at the SBC stage).\"}, {\"newText\": \"14:- **Compatibility filtering** (declared in `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::Compatibility`): 46 raw pairings reduced to 34 real configs — pruned 12 on battery↔airframe cell-count (P1, e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and 0 on thermal↔DVR video format (V2, a thermal whose output no DVR can record — CVBS via DVR1-6 or digital HDMI/USB via DVR7-9, now moot since DVR removed from architecture).\", \"oldText\": \"14:- **Compatibility filtering** (declared in `DroneSystemModel::Architecture::Compatibility`): 46 raw pairings reduced to 34 real configs — pruned 12 on battery↔airframe cell-count (P1, e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and 0 on thermal↔DVR video format (V2, a thermal whose output no DVR can record — CVBS via DVR1-6 or digital HDMI/USB via DVR7-9).\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/analysis/flight_time_results.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_39c7b1c0eef34542bcf3c04d","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"Ranked by **endurance-per-dollar** = max hover flight time (min) ÷ total system cost (USD) × 1000 — i.e. **minutes of hover per $1,000**. Only configs meeting R6 (≥ 30 min) and the thrust/feasibility check are ranked. Each entry lists the **complete system bill of materials** by actual product name. Peripherals shown as *included with airframe* are bundled in a BNF/PNP airframe (no separate part or cost); the DVR was an earlier-stage recorder removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording.","oldText":"Ranked by **endurance-per-dollar** = max hover flight time (min) ÷ total system cost (USD) × 1000 — i.e. **minutes of hover per $1,000**. Only configs meeting R6 (≥ 30 min) and the thrust/feasibility check are ranked. Each entry lists the **complete system bill of materials** by actual product name. Peripherals shown as *included with airframe* are bundled in a BNF/PNP airframe (no separate part or cost); the DVR is an earlier-stage recorder (counted in cost, excluded from flight time)."},{"newText":"26:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`)","oldText":"26:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)"}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"Ranked by **endurance-per-dollar** = max hover flight time (min) ÷ total system cost (USD) × 1000 — i.e. **minutes of hover per $1,000**. Only configs meeting R6 (≥ 30 min) and the thrust/feasibility check are ranked. Each entry lists the **complete system bill of materials** by actual product name. Peripherals shown as *included with airframe* are bundled in a BNF/PNP airframe (no separate part or cost); the DVR was an earlier-stage recorder removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording.\", \"oldText\": \"Ranked by **endurance-per-dollar** = max hover flight time (min) ÷ total system cost (USD) × 1000 — i.e. **minutes of hover per $1,000**. Only configs meeting R6 (≥ 30 min) and the thrust/feasibility check are ranked. Each entry lists the **complete system bill of materials** by actual product name. Peripherals shown as *included with airframe* are bundled in a BNF/PNP airframe (no separate part or cost); the DVR is an earlier-stage recorder (counted in cost, excluded from flight time).\"}, {\"newText\": \"26:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`)\", \"oldText\": \"26:- Thermal camera: PurpleRiver Mini 640 (`T13`) · SBC: NanoPi M5 (4 GB) (`SBC3`) · DVR: Monster UVC Recorder (standalone USB-UVC DVR) (`DVR9`)\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":2484,"output":3074,"cacheRead":73472,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":70,"totalTokens":79030,"cost":{"input":0.00024839999999999997,"output":0.0006148,"cacheRead":0.00146944,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00233264}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783265147061,"responseId":"gen-1783265147-drrJ4ZO8oYa7N6lj1Jp5"}}
