5 system** (well under the $2,500 cap).\n \n > **The authoritative, current list of selected vs open components is [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md).** Read it first.\n \n","firstChangedLine":28},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265251398}}
{"type":"message","id":"37e1f4c6","parentId":"e051a9ae","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:27:31.399Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_71c5b4d489744a169670d8e8","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  63 `part def`s with attributes, ports, and formal `satisfy` traceability:\n  64 - **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, ThermalVideoRecorder, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n  65 - **AerialThermalObservationSystem** — composes SurveillanceDrone + GroundControlStation + ViewingComputer; connects the wireless RF links; derives `totalCost` (the MacBook Air `ViewingComputer` is an external actor, excluded from cost).\n  66 - **GroundControlStation** — two-tier, laptop-based: `laptopLink` (ELRS USB dongle — primary control + telemetry) + `rcTx` (handheld radio — Phase-1/backup) + `VideoReceiver` + `UsbVideoCapture` + `groundAntenna` (5.8 GHz directional patch for video-link range margin).\n- 67 - Component defs — **Airframe** (incl. `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s`, `maxThrustPerMotor_g`, and a **physical-integration layer**: `payloadDeckLength_mm`/`payloadDeckWidth_mm`/`payloadCapacity_g`/`batteryMount`), **Battery** (energy, chemistry, cells, `length/width/height_mm`), **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **ThermalVideoRecorder** (CVBS + digital DVR variants), **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, **Antenna** (`gain_dBi`, band, polarization — feeds the RF link budget), **AntiSparkFilter** (inline XT60, in the drone power path), **Charger** (6S Li-ion/LiPo bench charger — ground-support equipment).\n+ 67 - Component defs — **Airframe** (incl. `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s`, `maxThrustPerMotor_g`, and a **physical-integration layer**: `payloadDeckLength_mm`/`payloadDeckWidth_mm`/`payloadCapacity_g`/`batteryMount`), **Battery** (energy, chemistry, cells, `length/width/height_mm`), **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, **Antenna** (`gain_dBi`, band, polarization — feeds the RF link budget), **AntiSparkFilter** (inline XT60, in the drone power path), **Charger** (6S Li-ion/LiPo bench charger — ground-support equipment).\n  68 - **Compatibility** (sub-package) — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s declaring which pairings are real (battery↔airframe cell-count **and connector**, video-format chain, RF band). The structure is validated by Syside; the **rules are executed by the flight-time sweep**.\n  69 \n  70 ### Analysis\n  71 A parametric verification layer (structure validated by Syside; numeric execution needs a SysML v2 engine — the Python model below is the high-fidelity counterpart):\n     ...","patch":"--- /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n+++ /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n@@ -63,9 +63,9 @@\n `part def`s with attributes, ports, and formal `satisfy` traceability:\n - **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, ThermalVideoRecorder, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n - **AerialThermalObservationSystem** — composes SurveillanceDrone + GroundControlStation + ViewingComputer; connects the wireless RF links; derives `totalCost` (the MacBook Air `ViewingComputer` is an external actor, excluded from cost).\n - **GroundControlStation** — two-tier, laptop-based: `laptopLink` (ELRS USB dongle — primary control + telemetry) + `rcTx` (handheld radio — Phase-1/backup) + `VideoReceiver` + `UsbVideoCapture` + `groundAntenna` (5.8 GHz directional patch for video-link range margin).\n-- Component defs — **Airframe** (incl. `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s`, `maxThrustPerMotor_g`, and a **physical-integration layer**: `payloadDeckLength_mm`/`payloadDeckWidth_mm`/`payloadCapacity_g`/`batteryMount`), **Battery** (energy, chemistry, cells, `length/width/height_mm`), **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **ThermalVideoRecorder** (CVBS + digital DVR variants), **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, **Antenna** (`gain_dBi`, band, polarization — feeds the RF link budget), **AntiSparkFilter** (inline XT60, in the drone power path), **Charger** (6S Li-ion/LiPo bench charger — ground-support equipment).\n+- Component defs — **Airframe** (incl. `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s`, `maxThrustPerMotor_g`, and a **physical-integration layer**: `payloadDeckLength_mm`/`payloadDeckWidth_mm`/`payloadCapacity_g`/`batteryMount`), **Battery** (energy, chemistry, cells, `length/width/height_mm`), **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, **Antenna** (`gain_dBi`, band, polarization — feeds the RF link budget), **AntiSparkFilter** (inline XT60, in the drone power path), **Charger** (6S Li-ion/LiPo bench charger — ground-support equipment).\n - **Compatibility** (sub-package) — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s declaring which pairings are real (battery↔airframe cell-count **and connector**, video-format chain, RF band). The structure is validated by Syside; the **rules are executed by the flight-time sweep**.\n \n ### Analysis\n A parametric verification layer (structure validated by Syside; numeric execution needs a SysML v2 engine — the Python model below is the high-fidelity counterpart):\n","firstChangedLine":67},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265251398}}
{"type":"message","id":"448aed4e","parentId":"37e1f4c6","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:27:31.399Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4f41dfbef35747babf0f93cc","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  81 \n  82 The market data — ~110 real options as typed usages with `:>>` value bindings, importing\n  83 the defs from `model.sysml`: **23 airframes** (22 with confirmed mass), **21 Li-ion battery\n  84 packs** (BAT01–BAT21), **16 thermal cameras**, **3 SBCs**, plus VTX, FPV cameras, GPS,\n- 85 receivers, DVRs, and ground video receivers. To add an option, add a typed usage here\n+ 85 receivers, and ground video receivers. To add an option, add a typed usage here\n  86 (not a new def).\n  87 \n  88 ## Flight-time & trade-study analysis (`analysis/flight_time_model.py`)\n  89 \n     ...","patch":"--- /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n+++ /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n@@ -81,9 +81,9 @@\n \n The market data — ~110 real options as typed usages with `:>>` value bindings, importing\n the defs from `model.sysml`: **23 airframes** (22 with confirmed mass), **21 Li-ion battery\n packs** (BAT01–BAT21), **16 thermal cameras**, **3 SBCs**, plus VTX, FPV cameras, GPS,\n-receivers, DVRs, and ground video receivers. To add an option, add a typed usage here\n+receivers, and ground video receivers. To add an option, add a typed usage here\n (not a new def).\n \n ## Flight-time & trade-study analysis (`analysis/flight_time_model.py`)\n \n","firstChangedLine":85},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265251399}}
{"type":"message","id":"1edd1d58","parentId":"448aed4e","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:27:31.399Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_047485018c0b4edabafb3cea","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  90 A high-fidelity multirotor **endurance model integrated with the SysML model** — it *reads*\n  91 `candidates.sysml`, runs a holistic configuration sweep, and *writes back* ranked results.\n  92 \n  93 - **Physics:** momentum / actuator-disk theory + a forward-flight parasitic-drag term (same family as eCalc; FoM 0.65, η 0.80, ρ 1.225, Cd 1.0). Reports hover, cruise, and headwind endurance + a per-motor thrust feasibility check.\n- 94 - **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count, **V2** thermal↔DVR video format. The DVR is excluded from max-flight-time (it's a Phase 1–2 part; the SBC records at Phase 3) but kept for earlier-stage compatibility + cost.\n+ 94 - **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count. DVR compatibility filter removed (DVR dropped from architecture 2026-07-05 — SBC handles recording).\n  95 - **Cost + ground station:** per-component + drone + total-system cost, with bundled BNF/PNP peripherals at $0. The **ground video receiver is matched per-airframe to the VTX video format** (analog VRX for analog VTX; DJI/Walksnail goggles for digital air units).\n  96 - **Physical-integration check:** whether the **SBC physically fits** the airframe's usable top deck — a 3-tier verdict (fits / marginal / no-fit) from the deck/SBC dimensions.\n  97 - **Design locks:** the sweep fixes the thermal (`T13`), SBC (`SBC3`), and airframe (`AF3a`/`AF3b`, Chimera9 ECO) to the locked selections via `FIXED_*` constants (set to `None` to re-open a dimension).\n  98 \n     ...","patch":"--- /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n+++ /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n@@ -90,9 +90,9 @@\n A high-fidelity multirotor **endurance model integrated with the SysML model** — it *reads*\n `candidates.sysml`, runs a holistic configuration sweep, and *writes back* ranked results.\n \n - **Physics:** momentum / actuator-disk theory + a forward-flight parasitic-drag term (same family as eCalc; FoM 0.65, η 0.80, ρ 1.225, Cd 1.0). Reports hover, cruise, and headwind endurance + a per-motor thrust feasibility check.\n-- **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count, **V2** thermal↔DVR video format. The DVR is excluded from max-flight-time (it's a Phase 1–2 part; the SBC records at Phase 3) but kept for earlier-stage compatibility + cost.\n+- **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count. DVR compatibility filter removed (DVR dropped from architecture 2026-07-05 — SBC handles recording).\n - **Cost + ground station:** per-component + drone + total-system cost, with bundled BNF/PNP peripherals at $0. The **ground video receiver is matched per-airframe to the VTX video format** (analog VRX for analog VTX; DJI/Walksnail goggles for digital air units).\n - **Physical-integration check:** whether the **SBC physically fits** the airframe's usable top deck — a 3-tier verdict (fits / marginal / no-fit) from the deck/SBC dimensions.\n - **Design locks:** the sweep fixes the thermal (`T13`), SBC (`SBC3`), and airframe (`AF3a`/`AF3b`, Chimera9 ECO) to the locked selections via `FIXED_*` constants (set to `None` to re-open a dimension).\n \n","firstChangedLine":94},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265251399}}
{"type":"message","id":"036ca66c","parentId":"1edd1d58","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:27:31.400Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_229a5fdad7854f1299bafedc","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 106 ## Build roadmap (`systems_engineering_plan.md`)\n 107 \n 108 Three incremental phases: **(1)** basic LOS manual flight + FPV/analog video downlink to the\n 109 laptop + GPS waypoint routes (airframe + ELRS + battery + VRX/antenna + GPS + dongle) →\n-110 **(2)** thermal camera + onboard DVR recording → **(3)** onboard SBC detection/classification\n+110 **(2)** thermal camera + SBC onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink → **(3)** AI detection/autonomous route modification (software-only, no new hardware).\n 111 + autonomous route modification via MAVLink.\n 112 \n 113 ## Tooling\n 114 \n     ...","patch":"--- /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n+++ /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n@@ -106,9 +106,9 @@\n ## Build roadmap (`systems_engineering_plan.md`)\n \n Three incremental phases: **(1)** basic LOS manual flight + FPV/analog video downlink to the\n laptop + GPS waypoint routes (airframe + ELRS + battery + VRX/antenna + GPS + dongle) →\n-**(2)** thermal camera + onboard DVR recording → **(3)** onboard SBC detection/classification\n+**(2)** thermal camera + SBC onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink → **(3)** AI detection/autonomous route modification (software-only, no new hardware).\n + autonomous route modification via MAVLink.\n \n ## Tooling\n \n","firstChangedLine":110},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265251399}}
{"type":"message","id":"b07f6581","parentId":"036ca66c","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:27:48.699Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, README.md is done. Now CLAUDE.md and MODEL_ISSUES.md.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Now CLAUDE.md — the DVR references there"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b358a45aaae9412c80fd4738","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"**Onboard thermal recording** via the onboard SBC (`SingleBoardComputerPayload`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. The SBC records from the thermal camera via USB-UVC, eliminating the need for a standalone DVR.","oldText":"**Onboard thermal recording** via an inline DVR (`ThermalVideoRecorder`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. CVBS DVRs (DVR1-6, CVBS-in → microSD → pass-through to VTX) cover analog thermals; digital DVRs (DVR7-9: HDMI/USB-UVC) cover digital-output thermals. The DVR is an **earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part only** — at the SBC stage (Phase 3) the SBC records, so the DVR is excluded from max-flight-time but retained for camera↔DVR compatibility and cost."},{"newText":"2. EO/IR thermal camera + SBC onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink.\n3. On-board SBC AI detection (NanoPi M5) + autonomous route modification via MAVLink (software-only, no new hardware).","oldText":"2. EO/IR thermal camera + onboard DVR recording.\n3. On-board SBC detection (NanoPi M5) + autonomous route modification via MAVLink."},{"newText":"**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording, so no V2 compatibility filter is needed. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro).","oldText":"**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and **V2** thermal↔DVR (a thermal no DVR can record — raw SPI/CMOS — is dropped). The **DVR is not crossed and is excluded from flight time**: it is an earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part, so the headline endurance is the SBC-stage build (SBC present, DVR removed); the DVR is kept only for earlier-stage camera↔DVR compatibility and for cost. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro)."}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"**Onboard thermal recording** via the onboard SBC (`SingleBoardComputerPayload`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. The SBC records from the thermal camera via USB-UVC, eliminating the need for a standalone DVR.\", \"oldText\": \"**Onboard thermal recording** via an inline DVR (`ThermalVideoRecorder`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. CVBS DVRs (DVR1-6, CVBS-in → microSD → pass-through to VTX) cover analog thermals; digital DVRs (DVR7-9: HDMI/USB-UVC) cover digital-output thermals. The DVR is an **earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part only** — at the SBC stage (Phase 3) the SBC records, so the DVR is excluded from max-flight-time but retained for camera↔DVR compatibility and cost.\"}, {\"newText\": \"2. EO/IR thermal camera + SBC onboard recording + OpenHD digital downlink.\\n3. On-board SBC AI detection (NanoPi M5) + autonomous route modification via MAVLink (software-only, no new hardware).\", \"oldText\": \"2. EO/IR thermal camera + onboard DVR recording.\\n3. On-board SBC detection (NanoPi M5) + autonomous route modification via MAVLink.\"}, {\"newText\": \"**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording, so no V2 compatibility filter is needed. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro).\", \"oldText\": \"**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and **V2** thermal↔DVR (a thermal no DVR can record — raw SPI/CMOS — is dropped). The **DVR is not crossed and is excluded from flight time**: it is an earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part, so the headline endurance is the SBC-stage build (SBC present, DVR removed); the DVR is kept only for earlier-stage camera↔DVR compatibility and for cost. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro).\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":3819,"output":1174,"cacheRead":81920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":20,"totalTokens":869