{"type":"message","id":"0616e3a3","parentId":"bf3386a3","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:27:55.099Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7a8adf41c85840e6b59a285f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- **DATA GAP — thermal module pricing is wide/uncertain** (factory-direct Chinese\n  modules, InfiRay street pricing). Representative midpoints used.\n- **RESOLVED (documented) — RunCam Mini DVR two price points** ($17.99 direct /\n  $29.99 Amazon); modeled once at the direct price (DVR1). No further action.\n- **RESOLVED (documented) — EasyCAP capture (VC4)** is only *partially* macOS-\n  compatible (driver issues, not true UVC); modeled as `macOsCompatible = false`.\n- **DATA GAP — several analog cameras** list estimated (`est`) illumination/power\n  values; bound as given, treat as approximate.\n\n---\n\n## E. Cross-reference note\n\n**RESOLVED (2026-06-26).** Markdown prose now references the correct model element\nnames. `README.md`'s Architecture section was rewritten to drop the removed\n`TelemetryTransmitter` / `TelemetryReceiver` parts (telemetry is carried by the\nELRS `RadioReceiver` / `RadioControlTransmitter`), fix the `SurveillanceDrone` and\n`GroundControlStation` compositions, and add the current parts (`FpvCamera`,\n`GpsModule`, `ThermalVideoRecorder`, `UsbVideoCapture`, the `Compatibility`\nsub-package, and the thermal-detection analysis defs). The `CameraSubsystem` →\n`CameraRequirements` package rename is reflected (README already listed\n`CameraRequirements`). Requirement IDs `R3_CAM_*` are unchanged.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265275099}}
{"type":"message","id":"7f4fccec","parentId":"0616e3a3","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:28:23.017Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to append the new DVR removal decision to MODEL_ISSUES.md. I'll add it after the existing last entry in section D (the RESOLVED items) and before section E.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e1d2dfb3e05f421b8e932969","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"- **RESOLVED (documented) — EasyCAP capture (VC4)** is only *partially* macOS-\n  compatible (driver issues, not true UVC); modeled as `macOsCompatible = false`.\n- **DATA GAP — several analog cameras** list estimated (`est`) illumination/power\n  values; bound as given, treat as approximate.\n\n---\n\n## F. Architectural changes\n\n13. **DECISION (2026-07-05) — DVR removed; SBC moved to Phase 2.**\n\n    - **Context:** David requested the standalone Monster UVC Recorder (`DVR9`) be\n      removed from the architecture entirely. Instead of a separate DVR, the SBC\n      (`SBC3`, NanoPi M5) handles onboard recording via USB-UVC from the T13\n      thermal camera — eliminating a $129 part and ~430 g of mass.\n    - **Phase restructure:**\n      - **Phase 2** (was: thermal + DVR + OpenHD) → becomes **thermal + SBC +\n        OpenHD**. The SBC and its mount/cooling are procured in Phase 2 alongside\n        the T13 and OpenHD hardware. Phase 2 subtotal: ~$936 (+$12 net from\n        dropping DVR $129 and adding SBC $141).\n      - **Phase 3** (was: SBC procurement → becomes: **AI software deployment**,\n        no new hardware procurement). All hardware is on-board since Phase 2.\n    - **Files changed (2026-07-05):**\n      - `model.sysml` — removed `part def ThermalVideoRecorder` and the\n        `recorder : ThermalVideoRecorder` part from `SurveillanceDrone`;\n        removed `camToRec` and `recToVtx` video interfaces; removed\n        `recorder` from `totalPower` rollup.\n      - `BOM.md` — DVR9 row removed; SBC3 + mount moved to Phase 2; Phase 3\n        marked as $0 software; totals recalculated.\n      - `systems_engineering_plan.md` — Phase 2 steps now include SBC mounting\n        + OpenHD config; Phase 3 is software-only.\n      - `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md` — DVR open item replaced with SBC-recording\n        note.\n      - `REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md` — phase descriptions updated.\n      - `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` — architecture description updated.\n      - `analysis/flight_time_results.md`,\n        `analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md` — prose updated to reflect\n        DVR removal.\n      - `candidates.sysml` — `part DVR9` retained as unused historical\n        candidate (no active references in the architecture).\n    - **Budget impact:** R4 system cost dropped from ~$2,088 to ~$1,960 (savings\n      of ~$128 from DVR removal, partially offset by SBC moving to Phase 2\n      costing). Grand total ~$2,290.75 vs ~$2,419.75 previously.","oldText":"- **RESOLVED (documented) — EasyCAP capture (VC4)** is only *partially* macOS-\n  compatible (driver issues, not true UVC); modeled as `macOsCompatible = false`.\n- **DATA GAP — several analog cameras** list estimated (`est`) illumination/power\n  values; bound as given, treat as approximate."}],"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/MODEL_ISSUES.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"edits\": [{\"newText\": \"- **RESOLVED (documented) — EasyCAP capture (VC4)** is only *partially* macOS-\\n  compatible (driver issues, not true UVC); modeled as `macOsCompatible = false`.\\n- **DATA GAP — several analog cameras** list estimated (`est`) illumination/power\\n  values; bound as given, treat as approximate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## F. Architectural changes\\n\\n13. **DECISION (2026-07-05) — DVR removed; SBC moved to Phase 2.**\\n\\n    - **Context:** David requested the standalone Monster UVC Recorder (`DVR9`) be\\n      removed from the architecture entirely. Instead of a separate DVR, the SBC\\n      (`SBC3`, NanoPi M5) handles onboard recording via USB-UVC from the T13\\n      thermal camera — eliminating a $129 part and ~430 g of mass.\\n    - **Phase restructure:**\\n      - **Phase 2** (was: thermal + DVR + OpenHD) → becomes **thermal + SBC +\\n        OpenHD**. The SBC and its mount/cooling are procured in Phase 2 alongside\\n        the T13 and OpenHD hardware. Phase 2 subtotal: ~$936 (+$12 net from\\n        dropping DVR $129 and adding SBC $141).\\n      - **Phase 3** (was: SBC procurement → becomes: **AI software deployment**,\\n        no new hardware procurement). All hardware is on-board since Phase 2.\\n    - **Files changed (2026-07-05):**\\n      - `model.sysml` — removed `part def ThermalVideoRecorder` and the\\n        `recorder : ThermalVideoRecorder` part from `SurveillanceDrone`;\\n        removed `camToRec` and `recToVtx` video interfaces; removed\\n        `recorder` from `totalPower` rollup.\\n      - `BOM.md` — DVR9 row removed; SBC3 + mount moved to Phase 2; Phase 3\\n        marked as $0 software; totals recalculated.\\n      - `systems_engineering_plan.md` — Phase 2 steps now include SBC mounting\\n        + OpenHD config; Phase 3 is software-only.\\n      - `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md` — DVR open item replaced with SBC-recording\\n        note.\\n      - `REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md` — phase descriptions updated.\\n      - `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` — architecture description updated.\\n      - `analysis/flight_time_results.md`,\\n        `analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md` — prose updated to reflect\\n        DVR removal.\\n      - `candidates.sysml` — `part DVR9` retained as unused historical\\n        candidate (no active references in the architecture).\\n    - **Budget impact:** R4 system cost dropped from ~$2,088 to ~$1,960 (savings\\n      of ~$128 from DVR removal, partially offset by SBC moving to Phase 2\\n      costing). Grand total ~$2,290.75 vs ~$2,419.75 previously.\", \"oldText\": \"- **RESOLVED (documented) — EasyCAP capture (VC4)** is only *partially* macOS-\\n  compatible (driver issues, not true UVC); modeled as `macOsCompatible = false`.\\n- **DATA GAP — several analog cameras** list estimated (`est`) illumination/power\\n  values; bound as given, treat as approximate.\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/MODEL_ISSUES.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":85285,"output":929,"cacheRead":2048,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":42,"totalTokens":88262,"cost":{"input":0.0085285,"output":0.0001858,"cacheRead":0.00004096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.008755259999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783265275102,"responseId":"gen-1783265275-dh358QsUCvlKuJ8SmFZm"}}
