{"type":"message","id":"367f964e","parentId":"ebb3dbc8","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:33:33.479Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_a825e1791f3d41dea4fe82c1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== Phase 2/3 totals in BOM ===\n## Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink\n\n--\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$936.00** |\n\n## Phase 3 — AI detection + autonomous route modification (software)\n\n--\n| All hardware on-board since Phase 2. Phase 3 is software-only: deploy INT8-quantized model via RKNN toolchain, integrate MAVLink autonomous route modification. | — | — | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$0.00** |\n\n=== Totals section ===\n## Totals\n\n| Phase | Subtotal |\n|---|---|\n| Phase 1 — flight + FPV + waypoints | $1,354.75 |\n| Phase 2 — thermal + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink | ~$936.00 |\n| Phase 3 — AI deployment (software only) | $0.00 |\n| **Grand total (all procurement)** | **~$2,290.75** |"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":8,"aggregated":"=== Phase 2/3 totals in BOM ===\n## Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink\n\n--\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$936.00** |\n\n## Phase 3 — AI detection + autonomous route modification (software)\n\n--\n| All hardware on-board since Phase 2. Phase 3 is software-only: deploy INT8-quantized model via RKNN toolchain, integrate MAVLink autonomous route modification. | — | — | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$0.00** |\n\n=== Totals section ===\n## Totals\n\n| Phase | Subtotal |\n|---|---|\n| Phase 1 — flight + FPV + waypoints | $1,354.75 |\n| Phase 2 — thermal + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink | ~$936.00 |\n| Phase 3 — AI deployment (software only) | $0.00 |\n| **Grand total (all procurement)** | **~$2,290.75** |","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265613478}}
{"type":"message","id":"1379bf43","parentId":"367f964e","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:33:41.472Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Everything looks clean. Let me also quickly verify the other files that were updated - `analysis/flight_time_results.md`, `analysis/flight_time_value_ranking.md`, `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md`, and `SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md` for any remaining DVR references.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_380bb08a50d24baa82ae142c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && echo \"=== DVR in analysis/ ===\" && grep -rn \"DVR\\|standalone DVR\\|UVC Recorder\\|ThermalVideoRecorder\" analysis/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \"=== REQUIREMENTS ===\" && grep -n \"DVR\\|standalone\" REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \"=== CLAUDE ===\" && grep -n \"DVR\\|ThermalVideoRecorder\\|standalone DVR\" CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \"=== README ===\" && grep -n \"DVR\\|ThermalVideoRecorder\\|standalone DVR\" README.md 2>/dev/null | head -5"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && echo \\\"=== DVR in analysis/ ===\\\" && grep -rn \\\"DVR\\\\|standalone DVR\\\\|UVC Recorder\\\\|ThermalVideoRecorder\\\" analysis/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \\\"=== REQUIREMENTS ===\\\" && grep -n \\\"DVR\\\\|standalone\\\" REQUIREMENTS_EXPORT_26_06_30.md 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \\\"=== CLAUDE ===\\\" && grep -n \\\"DVR\\\\|ThermalVideoRecorder\\\\|standalone DVR\\\" CLAUDE.md 2>/dev/null | head -5 && echo \\\"=== README ===\\\" && grep -n \\\"DVR\\\\|ThermalVideoRecorder\\\\|standalone DVR\\\" README.md 2>/dev/null | head -5\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":438,"output":304,"cacheRead":90624,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":75,"totalTokens":91366,"cost":{"input":0.0000438,"output":0.0000608,"cacheRead":0.00181248,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00191708}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783265613486,"responseId":"gen-1783265614-goYx6VdtyBeuJAc28ZxR"}}
{"type":"message","id":"da91d2dd","parentId":"1379bf43","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:33:41.498Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_380bb08a50d24baa82ae142c","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== DVR in analysis/ ===\n=== REQUIREMENTS ===\n221:- **Acronyms:** AGL (above ground level), LWIR (long-wave infrared), NETD (noise-equivalent temperature difference), SBC (single-board computer), GCS (ground control station), VTX/VRX (video transmitter/receiver), DVR (digital video recorder), ELRS (ExpressLRS), CRSF (Crossfire serial protocol), CVBS (composite analog video), LOS (line of sight), COTS (commercial off-the-shelf), MTOM (max takeoff mass).\n=== CLAUDE ===\n32:- **Architecture** — `part def`s for each component (`Airframe`, `Battery`, `CameraSubsystem`, `FpvCamera`, `GpsModule`, `SingleBoardComputerPayload`, `RadioReceiver`, `VideoTransmitter`, `ThermalVideoRecorder`, `VideoReceiver`, `UsbVideoCapture`, etc.). Each part carries `attribute`s (cost_USD, mass, power…), `port`s, and formal `satisfy` statements linking it back to the requirements it fulfills. `SurveillanceDrone` composes the airborne parts and wires them with `interface connect`; `AerialThermalObservationSystem` composes drone + `GroundControlStation` + `ViewingComputer` and connects the wireless RF links. Derived attributes (`totalPower`, `totalCost`, `subTotalCost`) roll up from the leaf parts. A **`Compatibility`** sub-package (added 2026-06-26) declares which component pairings form a *real* configuration as formal SysML v2 — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s for the battery↔airframe cell-count rule (P1), the video-format chain (V1–V4), and RF band (R1–R2). `Airframe` carries `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s` for the voltage rule. The component part defs' power/video/RF ports are **typed** to these port defs, and the battery-power + video connects in `SurveillanceDrone` are typed to their interface defs (data/GNSS ports stay untyped). Syside validates the structure; the **rules are enforced by the flight-time sweep** (`model.sysml` declares, `flight_time_model.py` executes — see §C11-C12 in [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\n46:- **Onboard thermal recording** via the onboard SBC (`SingleBoardComputerPayload`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. The SBC records from the thermal camera via USB-UVC, eliminating the need for a standalone DVR.\n65:**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording, so no V2 compatibility filter is needed. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro). **Recommended baseline:** DarwinFPV 129 (AF9a) + 4S 12Ah Amprius + T13 + SBC3 → 69.1 min hover, ~$1,505 system (well under the $2,500 R4 cap). (The earlier KOLAS7 \"71 min winner\" was a data artifact — its modeled mass omitted the 188 g of motors; corrected to as-built ~540–565 g, see `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §D.) See also `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C11-C12.\n79:Cost is computed in the sweep too (per-component + drone total + total system incl. a laptop-based GCS); bundled VTX/FPV/GPS/RX add $0 (already in the airframe price) and the DVR is included for cost. **The GCS ground video receiver is matched per-airframe to the VTX video format** (`MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C15): GCS = base $81 (backup radio + ELRS control dongle) + the cheapest compatible VRX — **CVBS → Skydroid $45, DJI → Goggles N3 $230, Walksnail → Goggles L $199** (`vrx_by_format` in `flight_time_model.py`; CSV cols `video_format`/`gcs_vrx_name`/`gcs_vrx_cost`). Analog frames are unaffected; the 7 DJI-air-unit frames carry the $230 goggles (+$185 system). All top-100 endurance configs sit under the R4 $2,500 cap (analog ~$820–$1,360 system; the digital AF12 CineLR 7 O4 is the lone frame that reaches ~$2,497, right at the cap).\n=== README ===\n64:- **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, ThermalVideoRecorder, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n94:- **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count. DVR compatibility filter removed (DVR dropped from architecture 2026-07-05 — SBC handles recording)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":11,"aggregated":"=== DVR in analysis/ ===\n=== REQUIREMENTS ===\n221:- **Acronyms:** AGL (above ground level), LWIR (long-wave infrared), NETD (noise-equivalent temperature difference), SBC (single-board computer), GCS (ground control station), VTX/VRX (video transmitter/receiver), DVR (digital video recorder), ELRS (ExpressLRS), CRSF (Crossfire serial protocol), CVBS (composite analog video), LOS (line of sight), COTS (commercial off-the-shelf), MTOM (max takeoff mass).\n=== CLAUDE ===\n32:- **Architecture** — `part def`s for each component (`Airframe`, `Battery`, `CameraSubsystem`, `FpvCamera`, `GpsModule`, `SingleBoardComputerPayload`, `RadioReceiver`, `VideoTransmitter`, `ThermalVideoRecorder`, `VideoReceiver`, `UsbVideoCapture`, etc.). Each part carries `attribute`s (cost_USD, mass, power…), `port`s, and formal `satisfy` statements linking it back to the requirements it fulfills. `SurveillanceDrone` composes the airborne parts and wires them with `interface connect`; `AerialThermalObservationSystem` composes drone + `GroundControlStation` + `ViewingComputer` and connects the wireless RF links. Derived attributes (`totalPower`, `totalCost`, `subTotalCost`) roll up from the leaf parts. A **`Compatibility`** sub-package (added 2026-06-26) declares which component pairings form a *real* configuration as formal SysML v2 — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s for the battery↔airframe cell-count rule (P1), the video-format chain (V1–V4), and RF band (R1–R2). `Airframe` carries `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s` for the voltage rule. The component part defs' power/video/RF ports are **typed** to these port defs, and the battery-power + video connects in `SurveillanceDrone` are typed to their interface defs (data/GNSS ports stay untyped). Syside validates the structure; the **rules are enforced by the flight-time sweep** (`model.sysml` declares, `flight_time_model.py` executes — see §C11-C12 in [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\n46:- **Onboard thermal recording** via the onboard SBC (`SingleBoardComputerPayload`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. The SBC records from the thermal camera via USB-UVC, eliminating the need for a standalone DVR.\n65:**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording, so no V2 compatibility filter is needed. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro). **Recommended baseline:** DarwinFPV 129 (AF9a) + 4S 12Ah Amprius + T13 + SBC3 → 69.1 min hover, ~$1,505 system (well under the $2,500 R4 cap). (The earlier KOLAS7 \"71 min winner\" was a data artifact — its modeled mass omitted the 188 g of motors; corrected to as-built ~540–565 g, see `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §D.) See also `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C11-C12.\n79:Cost is computed in the sweep too (per-component + drone total + total system incl. a laptop-based GCS); bundled VTX/FPV/GPS/RX add $0 (already in the airframe price) and the DVR is included for cost. **The GCS ground video receiver is matched per-airframe to the VTX video format** (`MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C15): GCS = base $81 (backup radio + ELRS control dongle) + the cheapest compatible VRX — **CVBS → Skydroid $45, DJI → Goggles N3 $230, Walksnail → Goggles L $199** (`vrx_by_format` in `flight_time_model.py`; CSV cols `video_format`/`gcs_vrx_name`/`gcs_vrx_cost`). Analog frames are unaffected; the 7 DJI-air-unit frames carry the $230 goggles (+$185 system). All top-100 endurance configs sit under the R4 $2,500 cap (analog ~$820–$1,360 system; the digital AF12 CineLR 7 O4 is the lone frame that reaches ~$2,497, right at the cap).\n=== README ===\n64:- **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, ThermalVideoRecorder, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n94:- **Compatibility filtering (executes the model's rules):** **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count. DVR compatibility filter removed (DVR dropped from architecture 2026-07-05 — SBC handles recording).","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265621497}}
