S.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\", \"newText\": \"- Component defs — **Airframe**, **Battery**, **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, etc. Each part carries `attribute`s (cost_USD, mass, power…), `port`s, and formal `satisfy` statements linking it back to the requirements it fulfills. `SurveillanceDrone` composes the airborne parts and wires them with `interface connect`; `AerialThermalObservationSystem` composes drone + `GroundControlStation` + `ViewingComputer` and connects the wireless RF links. Derived attributes (`totalPower`, `totalCost`, `subTotalCost`) roll up from the leaf parts. A **`Compatibility`** sub-package (added 2026-06-26) declares which component pairings form a *real* configuration as formal SysML v2 — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s for the battery↔airframe cell-count rule (P1), the video-format chain (V1–V4), and RF band (R1–R2). `Airframe` carries `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s` for the voltage rule. The component part defs' power/video/RF ports are **typed** to these port defs, and the battery-power + video connects in `SurveillanceDrone` are typed to their interface defs (data/GNSS ports stay untyped). Syside validates the structure; the **rules are enforced by the flight-time sweep** (`model.sysml` declares, `flight_time_model.py` executes — see §C11-C12 in [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\"}], \"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_13fd93392a734ff7a18f9f49","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"Cost is computed in the sweep too (per-component + drone total + total system incl. a laptop-based GCS); bundled VTX/FPV/GPS/RX add $0 (already in the airframe price). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording.","oldText":"Cos