{"type":"message","id":"82011176","parentId":"69c3a86e","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:34:01.897Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f3db515160ad4f96bc045b04","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"error\",\n  \"tool\": \"edit\",\n  \"error\": \"Could not find the exact text in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md. The old text must match exactly including all whitespace and newlines.\\nCurrent file contents:\\n# CLAUDE.md\\n\\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\\n\\n## What this repository is\\n\\nThis is a **Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE)** project for a thermal surveillance drone (wildlife scouting), not a software codebase. There is no build, lint, or test toolchain — the \\\"source\\\" is engineering documentation: a SysML v2 textual model plus trade studies that evaluate real, commercially-available components against it. The work follows Agile MBSE with **git as the source of truth** for engineering decisions.\\n\\n> **Currently selected components — read [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md) first.** It is the single authoritative list of what is LOCKED vs OPEN (airframe, thermal camera, SBC, …). Locks are machine-enforced\\n... (truncated)\"\n}"}],"details":{"status":"error","tool":"edit","error":"Could not find the exact text in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/CLAUDE.md. The old text must match exactly including all whitespace and newlines.\nCurrent file contents:\n# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## What this repository is\n\nThis is a **Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE)** project for a thermal surveillance drone (wildlife scouting), not a software codebase. There is no build, lint, or test toolchain — the \"source\" is engineering documentation: a SysML v2 textual model plus trade studies that evaluate real, commercially-available components against it. The work follows Agile MBSE with **git as the source of truth** for engineering decisions.\n\n> **Currently selected components — read [`SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md`](SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md) first.** It is the single authoritative list of what is LOCKED vs OPEN (airframe, thermal camera, SBC, …). Locks are machine-enforced\n... (truncated)"},"isError":true,"timestamp":1783265641896}}
