{"type":"message","id":"9fa98cb0","parentId":"83226e1c","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:34:01.898Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e59cf104dc094c2b826ebe60","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  60 - Per-subsystem packages — `CameraRequirements`, `BatterySubsystem`, `SBCSubsystem`, `GCSSubsystem`, `AirframeSubsystem` — each tracing up to its parent mission requirement (e.g. `R3_CAM_FOV subsets R3`, cost reqs `subsets R4`). IDs follow `R<n>_<SUBSYS>_<NAME>`.\n  61 \n  62 ### Architecture\n  63 `part def`s with attributes, ports, and formal `satisfy` traceability:\n- 64 - **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, ThermalVideoRecorder, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n+ 64 - **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n  65 - **AerialThermalObservationSystem** — composes SurveillanceDrone + GroundControlStation + ViewingComputer; connects the wireless RF links; derives `totalCost` (the MacBook Air `ViewingComputer` is an external actor, excluded from cost).\n  66 - **GroundControlStation** — two-tier, laptop-based: `laptopLink` (ELRS USB dongle — primary control + telemetry) + `rcTx` (handheld radio — Phase-1/backup) + `VideoReceiver` + `UsbVideoCapture` + `groundAntenna` (5.8 GHz directional patch for video-link range margin).\n  67 - Component defs — **Airframe** (incl. `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s`, `maxThrustPerMotor_g`, and a **physical-integration layer**: `payloadDeckLength_mm`/`payloadDeckWidth_mm`/`payloadCapacity_g`/`batteryMount`), **Battery** (energy, chemistry, cells, `length/width/height_mm`), **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, **Antenna** (`gain_dBi`, band, polarization — feeds the RF link budget), **AntiSparkFilter** (inline XT60, in the drone power path), **Charger** (6S Li-ion/LiPo bench charger — ground-support equipment).\n  68 - **Compatibility** (sub-package) — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s declaring which pairings are real (battery↔airframe cell-count **and connector**, video-format chain, RF band). The structure is validated by Syside; the **rules are executed by the flight-time sweep**.\n     ...","patch":"--- /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n+++ /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/README.md\n@@ -60,9 +60,9 @@\n - Per-subsystem packages — `CameraRequirements`, `BatterySubsystem`, `SBCSubsystem`, `GCSSubsystem`, `AirframeSubsystem` — each tracing up to its parent mission requirement (e.g. `R3_CAM_FOV subsets R3`, cost reqs `subsets R4`). IDs follow `R<n>_<SUBSYS>_<NAME>`.\n \n ### Architecture\n `part def`s with attributes, ports, and formal `satisfy` traceability:\n-- **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, ThermalVideoRecorder, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n+- **SurveillanceDrone** — composes the airborne parts (Airframe, Battery, CameraSubsystem [thermal], FpvCamera, GpsModule, SingleBoardComputerPayload, RadioReceiver, VideoTransmitter) wired with typed power/video interfaces; derives `totalPower`.\n - **AerialThermalObservationSystem** — composes SurveillanceDrone + GroundControlStation + ViewingComputer; connects the wireless RF links; derives `totalCost` (the MacBook Air `ViewingComputer` is an external actor, excluded from cost).\n - **GroundControlStation** — two-tier, laptop-based: `laptopLink` (ELRS USB dongle — primary control + telemetry) + `rcTx` (handheld radio — Phase-1/backup) + `VideoReceiver` + `UsbVideoCapture` + `groundAntenna` (5.8 GHz directional patch for video-link range margin).\n - Component defs — **Airframe** (incl. `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s`, `maxThrustPerMotor_g`, and a **physical-integration layer**: `payloadDeckLength_mm`/`payloadDeckWidth_mm`/`payloadCapacity_g`/`batteryMount`), **Battery** (energy, chemistry, cells, `length/width/height_mm`), **CameraSubsystem** (thermal), **FpvCamera**, **GpsModule**, **SingleBoardComputerPayload**, **RadioReceiver**, **VideoTransmitter**, **VideoReceiver**, **UsbVideoCapture**, **Antenna** (`gain_dBi`, band, polarization — feeds the RF link budget), **AntiSparkFilter** (inline XT60, in the drone power path), **Charger** (6S Li-ion/LiPo bench charger — ground-support equipment).\n - **Compatibility** (sub-package) — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s declaring which pairings are real (battery↔airframe cell-count **and connector**, video-format chain, RF band). The structure is validated by Syside; the **rules are executed by the flight-time sweep**.\n","firstChangedLine":64},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265641897}}
{"type":"message","id":"05a7082f","parentId":"9fa98cb0","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:34:18.218Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The first CLAUDE.md edit failed. Let me read the exact text around line 32 to get the matching correct.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"CLAUDE.md first edit needs exact text match. Let me grab it:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e0a489db42ee400583386249","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && sed -n '28,35p' CLAUDE.md"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone && sed -n '28,35p' CLAUDE.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":93432,"output":116,"cacheRead":1024,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":24,"totalTokens":94572,"cost":{"input":0.0093432,"output":0.000023199999999999998,"cacheRead":0.00002048,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.009386879999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783265641901,"responseId":"gen-1783265642-F7WQXfM44E1of7V4Zdx2"}}
{"type":"message","id":"5127627e","parentId":"05a7082f","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:34:18.242Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e0a489db42ee400583386249","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A single SysML v2 textual file, one top-level `package DroneSystemModel` containing four sub-packages. Understanding how they interlock is the key to being productive here:\n\n- **Requirements** — Top-level mission requirements `R1`–`R8` (note: `R3_1`/`R3_2`, not `R3.1`/`R3.2` — dots are invalid identifiers), plus per-subsystem requirement packages (`CameraRequirements`, `BatterySubsystem`, `SBCSubsystem`, `GCSSubsystem`, `AirframeSubsystem`). Subsystem requirements use `subsets` to trace up to the mission requirement they decompose (e.g. `R3_CAM_FOV subsets R3`, cost requirements `subsets R4`). Requirement IDs follow `R<n>_<SUBSYS>_<NAME>` (e.g. `R4_AF_PAYLOAD`). (The requirements package is `CameraRequirements`, deliberately distinct from the `CameraSubsystem` *part def* to avoid a name collision.)\n- **Architecture** — `part def`s for each component (`Airframe`, `Battery`, `CameraSubsystem`, `FpvCamera`, `GpsModule`, `SingleBoardComputerPayload`, `RadioReceiver`, `VideoTransmitter`, `ThermalVideoRecorder`, `VideoReceiver`, `UsbVideoCapture`, etc.). Each part carries `attribute`s (cost_USD, mass, power…), `port`s, and formal `satisfy` statements linking it back to the requirements it fulfills. `SurveillanceDrone` composes the airborne parts and wires them with `interface connect`; `AerialThermalObservationSystem` composes drone + `GroundControlStation` + `ViewingComputer` and connects the wireless RF links. Derived attributes (`totalPower`, `totalCost`, `subTotalCost`) roll up from the leaf parts. A **`Compatibility`** sub-package (added 2026-06-26) declares which component pairings form a *real* configuration as formal SysML v2 — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s for the battery↔airframe cell-count rule (P1), the video-format chain (V1–V4), and RF band (R1–R2). `Airframe` carries `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s` for the voltage rule. The component part defs' power/video/RF ports are **typed** to these port defs, and the battery-power + video connects in `SurveillanceDrone` are typed to their interface defs (data/GNSS ports stay untyped). Syside validates the structure; the **rules are enforced by the flight-time sweep** (`model.sysml` declares, `flight_time_model.py` executes — see §C11-C12 in [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\n- **Analysis** — A full parametric verification layer: `calc def`s `FlightTimeCalc` (energy / power → flight time, typed `ScalarQuantityValue` since ISQ `/` doesn't narrow to `DurationValue`) and `ScoreCalc` (flight-time magnitude / cost, via `QuantityCalculations::ToReal`); `constraint def`s `BudgetLimit` (R4, ≤ $2,500), `MinFlightTimeReq` (R6, ≥ 1800 s), `StretchFlightTimeReq` (R8, ≥ 3600 s); and two `analysis def` cases — `MinFlightTimeCheck` (subject = system; `assert constraint` on R4 + R6, returns a boolean verdict) and `TradeSpaceEvaluation` (subject = candidate; computes score + asserts budget). Thermal detection is also modeled (B3): `calc def`s `GroundSampleDistance`/`PixelsAcrossTarget`, `constraint def`s `DetectionCriterion` (≥1.5 px)/`RecognitionCriterion` (≥4 px), and `analysis def`s `ThermalDetectionCheck` (120 m, R3_1) / `ThermalRecognitionCheck` (90 m, R3_2/R3_CAM_RES) — Johnson-criteria pixels-on-target. Requirement checks compare dimensionally (`flightTime >= 1800 [s]`). Battery energy must be in joules `[J]` (`Wh × 3600`). Syside validates structure but does not execute the calcs — numeric verdicts need a SysML v2 execution engine (see [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md) §A10).\n- **Views** (added 2026-06-27) — Four SysML v2 `view def` + `view` presentations that `expose` model slices by stakeholder concern: `operationalMission` (mission requirements + system context), `logicalArchitecture` (system/drone/GCS decomposition), `interfaceBehavior` (the `Compatibility` interface layer + connections), and `systemVerification` (the Analysis layer). Syside validates the structure; diagram/table rendering needs a SysML v2 viewer. **Gotcha:** `verification` (like `interface`, `view`, `analysis`) is a reserved keyword, so the usage is named `systemVerification`, not `verification`."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":6,"aggregated":"A single SysML v2 textual file, one top-level `package DroneSystemModel` containing four sub-packages. Understanding how they interlock is the key to being productive here:\n\n- **Requirements** — Top-level mission requirements `R1`–`R8` (note: `R3_1`/`R3_2`, not `R3.1`/`R3.2` — dots are invalid identifiers), plus per-subsystem requirement packages (`CameraRequirements`, `BatterySubsystem`, `SBCSubsystem`, `GCSSubsystem`, `AirframeSubsystem`). Subsystem requirements use `subsets` to trace up to the mission requirement they decompose (e.g. `R3_CAM_FOV subsets R3`, cost requirements `subsets R4`). Requirement IDs follow `R<n>_<SUBSYS>_<NAME>` (e.g. `R4_AF_PAYLOAD`). (The requirements package is `CameraRequirements`, deliberately distinct from the `CameraSubsystem` *part def* to avoid a name collision.)\n- **Architecture** — `part def`s for each component (`Airframe`, `Battery`, `CameraSubsystem`, `FpvCamera`, `GpsModule`, `SingleBoardComputerPayload`, `RadioReceiver`, `VideoTransmitter`, `ThermalVideoRecorder`, `VideoReceiver`, `UsbVideoCapture`, etc.). Each part carries `attribute`s (cost_USD, mass, power…), `port`s, and formal `satisfy` statements linking it back to the requirements it fulfills. `SurveillanceDrone` composes the airborne parts and wires them with `interface connect`; `AerialThermalObservationSystem` composes drone + `GroundControlStation` + `ViewingComputer` and connects the wireless RF links. Derived attributes (`totalPower`, `totalCost`, `subTotalCost`) roll up from the leaf parts. A **`Compatibility`** sub-package (added 2026-06-26) declares which component pairings form a *real* configuration as formal SysML v2 — typed `port def`s, `enum def`s (`VideoFormat`, `RfBand`), `constraint def`s, and `interface def`s for the battery↔airframe cell-count rule (P1), the video-format chain (V1–V4), and RF band (R1–R2). `Airframe` carries `minCells_s`/`maxCells_s` for the voltage rule. The component part defs' power/video/RF ports are **typed** to these port defs, and the battery-power + video connects in `SurveillanceDrone` are typed to their interface defs (data/GNSS ports stay untyped). Syside validates the structure; the **rules are enforced by the flight-time sweep** (`model.sysml` declares, `flight_time_model.py` executes — see §C11-C12 in [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md)).\n- **Analysis** — A full parametric verification layer: `calc def`s `FlightTimeCalc` (energy / power → flight time, typed `ScalarQuantityValue` since ISQ `/` doesn't narrow to `DurationValue`) and `ScoreCalc` (flight-time magnitude / cost, via `QuantityCalculations::ToReal`); `constraint def`s `BudgetLimit` (R4, ≤ $2,500), `MinFlightTimeReq` (R6, ≥ 1800 s), `StretchFlightTimeReq` (R8, ≥ 3600 s); and two `analysis def` cases — `MinFlightTimeCheck` (subject = system; `assert constraint` on R4 + R6, returns a boolean verdict) and `TradeSpaceEvaluation` (subject = candidate; computes score + asserts budget). Thermal detection is also modeled (B3): `calc def`s `GroundSampleDistance`/`PixelsAcrossTarget`, `constraint def`s `DetectionCriterion` (≥1.5 px)/`RecognitionCriterion` (≥4 px), and `analysis def`s `ThermalDetectionCheck` (120 m, R3_1) / `ThermalRecognitionCheck` (90 m, R3_2/R3_CAM_RES) — Johnson-criteria pixels-on-target. Requirement checks compare dimensionally (`flightTime >= 1800 [s]`). Battery energy must be in joules `[J]` (`Wh × 3600`). Syside validates structure but does not execute the calcs — numeric verdicts need a SysML v2 execution engine (see [`MODEL_ISSUES.md`](MODEL_ISSUES.md) §A10).\n- **Views** (added 2026-06-27) — Four SysML v2 `view def` + `view` presentations that `expose` model slices by stakeholder concern: `operationalMission` (mission requirements + system context), `logicalArchitecture` (system/drone/GCS decomposition), `interfaceBehavior` (the `Compatibility` interface layer + connections), and `systemVerification` (the Analysis layer). Syside validates the structure; diagram/table rendering needs a SysML v2 viewer. **Gotcha:** `verification` (like `interface`, `view`, `analysis`) is a reserved keyword, so the usage is named `systemVerification`, not `verification`.","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783265658241}}
