{"type":"message","id":"f7aacd24","parentId":"c7cf0c18","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:41:34.085Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9532e6c28ceb4e38afef5b80","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md:65:| **On-board recording** | **SBC does it** — NanoPi M5 (`SBC3`) records thermal footage via USB-UVC from the T13. No separate DVR needed. | `—` | 2026-07-05 | DVR9 removed; SBC moved to Phase 2 procurement | SBC handles recording + inference in a single device; eliminates DVR cost ($129) and mass. | **2** |\nCLAUDE.md:46:- **Onboard thermal recording** via the onboard SBC (`SingleBoardComputerPayload`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. The SBC records from the thermal camera via USB-UVC, eliminating the need for a standalone DVR.\nCLAUDE.md:65:**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording, so no V2 compatibility filter is needed. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro). **Recommended baseline:** DarwinFPV 129 (AF9a) + 4S 12Ah Amprius + T13 + SBC3 → 69.1 min hover, ~$1,505 system (well under the $2,500 R4 cap). (The earlier KOLAS7 \"71 min winner\" was a data artifact — its modeled mass omitted the 188 g of motors; corrected to as-built ~540–565 g, see `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §D.) See also `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C11-C12.\nCLAUDE.md:79:Cost is computed in the sweep too (per-component + drone total + total system incl. a laptop-based GCS); bundled VTX/FPV/GPS/RX add $0 (already in the airframe price). The DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05) — the SBC handles recording. **The GCS ground video receiver is matched per-airframe to the VTX video format** (`MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C15): GCS = base $81 (backup radio + ELRS control dongle) + the cheapest compatible VRX — **CVBS → Skydroid $45, DJI → Goggles N3 $230, Walksnail → Goggles L $199** (`vrx_by_format` in `flight_time_model.py`; CSV cols `video_format`/`gcs_vrx_name`/`gcs_vrx_cost`). Analog frames are unaffected; the 7 DJI-air-unit frames carry the $230 goggles (+$185 system). All top-100 endurance configs sit under the R4 $2,500 cap (analog ~$820–$1,360 system; the digital AF12 CineLR 7 O4 is the lone frame that reaches ~$2,497, right at the cap)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":7,"aggregated":"SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md:65:| **On-board recording** | **SBC does it** — NanoPi M5 (`SBC3`) records thermal footage via USB-UVC from the T13. No separate DVR needed. | `—` | 2026-07-05 | DVR9 removed; SBC moved to Phase 2 procurement | SBC handles recording + inference in a single device; eliminates DVR cost ($129) and mass. | **2** |\nCLAUDE.md:46:- **Onboard thermal recording** via the onboard SBC (`SingleBoardComputerPayload`) so footage survives RF signal loss, avoiding a second VTX. The SBC records from the thermal camera via USB-UVC, eliminating the need for a standalone DVR.\nCLAUDE.md:65:**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W per