7 DJI-air-unit frames carry the $230 goggles (+$185 system). All top-100 endurance configs sit under the R4 $2,500 cap (analog ~$820–$1,360 system; the digital AF12 CineLR 7 O4 is the lone frame that reaches ~$2,497, right at the cap).","cwd":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1783266094084}}
{"type":"message","id":"5ea822b6","parentId":"f7aacd24","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:41:53.944Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CLAUDE.md and SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md still contain mentions of DVR, but they're all in the context of \"DVR was removed\" — explaining the decision. This is acceptable documentation:\n\n- SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md: \"No separate DVR needed\" / \"DVR9 removed\" — explaining that DVR was removed, not specifying it as an active component\n- CLAUDE.md: \"the DVR was removed from the architecture (2026-07-05)\" — historical documentation of the change\n\nSince David said \"make sure the DVR is completely removed from the architecture\" and these are documentation notes explaining *why* they were removed, this is correct behavior. The grep is matching on the word \"DVR\" appearing in explanation text, not as an active architectural element.\n\nHowever, let me re-read the original request: \"Please make sure the DVR is completely removed from the architecture, SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md, BOM.md, and whatever other files.\"\n\nThen the follow-up: \"don't remove historical information. Just add the new decision to remove the DVR.\"\n\nSo the intent is:\n- Architecture files (model.sysml): completely removed ✅\n- SELECTED_COMPONENTS.md: no \"open DVR item\" — replaced with \"SBC does it\" note ✅ (the DVR reference here is explaining the decision)\n- BOM.md: DVR row removed from Phase 2 ✅ (remaining DVR references are explanatory notes)\n- CLAUDE.md: the DVR references are explaining the architectural decision — keeping them as documentation of the change is consistent with \"don't remove historical information\"\n\nThese are acceptable — they're explanatory documentation, not active architectural references. The architecture (model.sysml, interfaces, phases) is entirely clean.\n\nLet me verify the total re-calc is correct:\n- Phase 1: $1,354.75 (unchanged)\n- Phase 2: $650 (T13) + $126 (SBC3) + $15 (mount) + $20 (WLAN_