{"type":"message","id":"a45563b5","parentId":"e1073a66","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:47:26.291Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking what the Phase 2 components are now after the restructuring. Let me just read the current state of BOM.md and systems_engineering_plan.md to give them the accurate answer.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8ed41a424aae446796ffa03d","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md","offset":33,"limit":20},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/BOM.md\", \"offset\": 33, \"limit\": 20}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_82032aeba5764c36b66775f5","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/systems_engineering_plan.md","offset":45,"limit":40},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/home/david12daniel/.openclaw/agents/thermal-surveillance-drone/systems_engineering_plan.md\", \"offset\": 45, \"limit\": 40}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":112841,"output":226,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":41,"totalTokens":113067,"cost":{"input":0.0112841,"output":0.0000452,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0113293}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1783266421365,"responseId":"gen-1783266422-Q4CUvzt7PznTxQLAdj0i"}}
{"type":"message","id":"85c47e62","parentId":"a45563b5","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:47:26.337Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8ed41a424aae446796ffa03d","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm) | `T13` | [thermal-image.com](https://www.thermal-image.com/product/mini-640-uncooled-lwir-thermal-camera-module/) | $650.00 |\n| NanoPi M5, 4 GB SBC (Rockchip RK3576) — onboard recording + AI inference | `SBC3` | [friendlyelec.com](https://www.friendlyelec.com/index.php?route=product/product&path=69&product_id=309) | $126.00 |\n| SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + 30 mm fan + heat-set hardware) | — | fabricated ([reference/cad-resources.md](reference/cad-resources.md)) | ~$15.00 |\n| LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 RTL8812EU bare WiFi module (air side) + USB-A stub + 2× u.fl→RP-SMA pigtails | `WLAN_AIR1` | [aliexpress.com](https://www.aliexpress.com/item/1005007098141054.html) | ~$20.00 |\n| Alfa AWUS036ACH RTL8812AU USB-C WiFi adapter (ground side) | `WLAN_GND1` | [rokland.com](https://store.rokland.com/products/alfa-awus036ach-usb-c-802-11ac-ac1200-dual-band-high-power-wifi-usb-adapter) | $65.00 |\n| Foxeer Echo 2 Max 5.8 GHz linear patch antenna × 2 (ground diversity, 60° beam, RP-SMA male) | `ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2` | [foxeer.com](https://www.foxeer.com/foxeer-echo-2-max-high-gain-antenna-g-434) | $60.00 |\n| VMware Fusion (ground station VM — free personal use) | — | vmware.com | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 2 subtotal** | | | **~$936.00** |\n\n## Phase 3 — AI detection + autonomous route modification (software)\n\n| Product | Part # | Link | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| All hardware on-board since Phase 2. Phase 3 is software-only: deploy INT8-quantized model via RKNN toolchain, integrate MAVLink autonomous route modification. | — | — | $0.00 |\n| **Phase 3 subtotal** | | | **$0.00** |\n\n\n[40 more lines in file. Use offset=53 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783266446337}}
{"type":"message","id":"d7862704","parentId":"85c47e62","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:47:26.338Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_82032aeba5764c36b66775f5","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Phase 2 — EO/IR Thermal Camera + SBC Onboard Recording + OpenHD Digital Downlink\n**Goal** — Mount the thermal camera and SBC, record onboard via SBC, and downlink live thermal video via OpenHD.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 1)**\n- Thermal Camera Subsystem — **PurpleRiver Mini 640** (`T13`, 640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm lens, USB)\n- Single-Board Computer — **NanoPi M5, 4 GB** (`SBC3`, Rockchip RK3576, RKNN NPU) — handles onboard recording + future AI inference\n- SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck + fan — see [`reference/cad-resources.md`](reference/cad-resources.md))\n- WiFi adapter (air) — LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 (`WLAN_AIR1`) for OpenHD digital downlink\n- WiFi adapter (ground) — Alfa AWUS036ACH (`WLAN_GND1`) for OpenHD reception\n- Ground diversity antennas — Foxeer Echo 2 Max × 2 (`ANT_GND1` + `ANT_GND2`)\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — all of Phase 1, plus the thermal camera, SBC (with mount/cooling), and OpenHD digital downlink hardware.\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Mount the thermal camera on the airframe (clear FOV, nose/chin) and power from the airframe rail.\n2. Mount the SBC on a 3D-printed deck; connect to the airframe rail and the flight controller (UART/MAVLink).\n3. Route the thermal camera video → SBC (USB-UVC for recording + future inference).\n4. Configure the SBC to record thermal footage to onboard storage (microSD/eMMC) on power-up.\n5. Configure OpenHD digital downlink: SBC encodes H.264 → WiFi air module transmits WFB-ng protocol → ground WiFi adapter + Foxeer antennas receive on laptop VM.\n6. Fly and recover thermal footage from SBC post-flight (footage survives RF loss).\n7. Confirm live thermal downlink on the laptop and Johnson detect/recognize performance at 90–120 m.\n\n**Result** — Thermal video recorded onboard via SBC (survives signal loss) with OpenHD digital downlink; meets the R3 detection/recognition requirements. No separate DVR required.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3 — AI Detection + Autonomous Route Modification (Software)\n**Goal** — Deploy on-board AI thermal detection/classification and dynamic mission adaptation using the SBC already on-board.\n\n**New Components (vs Phase 2)** — None (all hardware on-board since Phase 2).\n\n**Components Required (full list)** — same as Phase 2 (hardware).\n\n**Phase Steps**\n1. Deploy the INT8-quantized detection/classification model via the RKNN toolchain (RKNPU2); verify ≥ ~25 fps.\n2. Map detections to MAVLink commands (loiter/adjust on a target); modify the mission in-flight.\n3. Validate fallback: if the SBC fails, the drone completes the current waypoint and RTLs.\n\n**Result** — Autonomous drone that detects and reacts to thermal targets, meeting all SBC and camera requirements.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1783266446337}}
{"type":"message","id":"e9dfb06f","parentId":"d7862704","timestamp":"2026-07-05T15:47:35.826Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking what the Phase 2 components are now. Let me just present the info clearly.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_details"},{"type":"text","text":"Here's the current Phase 2 breakdown:\n\n**Phase 2 — EO/IR thermal camera + SBC + OpenHD digital downlink** (~$936)\n\n| # | Part # | Product | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `T13` | PurpleRiver Mini 640 thermal camera (640×512, 12 µm, 13 mm) | $650.00 |\n| 2 | `SBC3` | NanoPi M5, 4 GB SBC — handles onboard recording + AI inference | $126.00 |\n| 3 | — | SBC mount + cooling (3D-printed deck, 30 mm fan, hardware) | ~$15.00 |\n| 4 | `WLAN_AIR1` | LB-LINK BL-M8812EU2 WiFi module (air-side OpenHD) | ~$20.00 |\n| 5 | `WLAN_GND1` | Alfa AWUS036ACH WiFi adapter (ground-side OpenHD) | $65.00 |\n| 6 | `ANT_GND1`+`ANT_GND2` | Foxeer Echo 2 Max patch antennas × 2 (ground diversity) | $60.00 |\n\n**No DVR** — the SBC records thermal footage from the T13 via USB-UVC. No separate recorder needed.\n\n**Integration flow:**\n1. Mount T13 (nose/chin) + mount SBC on 3D-printed deck → connect to FC via UART/MAVLink\n2. Route T13 video → SBC via USB-UVC (recording + future inference)\n3. SBC encodes H.264 → WiFi air module transmits WFB-ng → ground WiFi + Foxeer antennas → laptop VM\n4. Recover footage from SBC storage post-flight (survives RF loss)\n\n**Phase 3** is then software-only — deploy the RKNN model, wire detections to MAVLink, no new hardware."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":114437,"output":434,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoningTokens":21,"totalTokens":114871,"cost":{"input":0.0114437,"output":0.0000868,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011530499999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783266446342,"responseId":"gen-1783266448-quDibp15FKcyZ6s0xcmo"}}
